symbol": "class", "gloss": "Code class: CODE_SYMBOL.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "function", "gloss": "Code function: CODE_SYMBOL.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code call: CODE_SYMBOL.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "argument", "gloss": "Code argument description: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Code assertion/change condition: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Bug reproduction: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected behavior: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Observed behavior: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "environment", "gloss": "Runtime environment: transitional STRING.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform: entity-descriptor platform facet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "test_id", "gloss": "Specific test identifier: CODE_SYMBOL.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Search flights from Tel Aviv to Berlin next Tuesday for two passengers.", "braincode": "ACTION search_travel(origin=\"Tel Aviv\", destination=\"Berlin\", date=\"2025-06-10\", passengers=2) -> flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Repairs the false exhaustive-index claim by indexing every current and newly added Action, UTTER, GENERATE, and TASK-context attribute with its value class.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "entity-descriptor", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical entity, location, state, positional, modifier, and platform symbols. Its composition rule distinguishes entity instances such as full and empty rolls without using prose.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mug", "gloss": "A large drinking cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet_paper_roll", "gloss": "A roll of toilet paper.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sponge", "gloss": "A cleaning sponge.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bowl", "gloss": "A bowl.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mirror", "gloss": "A reflective household item.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sink", "gloss": "A washing basin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "counter", "gloss": "A countertop surface.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cupboard", "gloss": "A storage cabinet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "refrigerator", "gloss": "A cooling storage appliance.", "nl_synonyms": ["fridge"]}, {"symbol": "full", "gloss": "State: containing its normal contents.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "empty", "gloss": "State: containing no relevant contents.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bottom_left", "gloss": "Positional qualifier: lower-left among comparable locations.", "nl_synonyms": ["lower left"]}, {"symbol": "red", "gloss": "Color modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "gray", "gloss": "Color modifier.", "nl_synonyms": ["grey"]}, {"symbol": "round", "gloss": "Shape modifier.", "nl_synonyms": ["circular"]}, {"symbol": "windows", "gloss": "Platform: Microsoft Windows.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A generic entity or location is lowercase_underscore. A describable instance is [state '_'] [position '_'] [modifier '_'] entity, with at most one member from each facet in that fixed order; omitted facets are absent. Thus full_toilet_paper_roll and bottom_left_cupboard are defined derived symbols. Additional entity, location, state, position, modifier, and platform members may be added under their named facet.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Move a full roll and an empty roll to the counter.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=full_toilet_paper_roll) -> full_toilet_paper_roll : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=full_toilet_paper_roll, destination=counter, relation=on)\nACTION pick_up(target=empty_toilet_paper_roll) -> empty_toilet_paper_roll : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=empty_toilet_paper_roll, destination=counter, relation=on)"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds separately look-upable entity and instance/state semantics, including a deterministic composition rule for sampled household distinctions.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "spatial-relation", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of relations used when placing one entity relative to another.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "in", "gloss": "Contained within.", "nl_synonyms": ["inside"]}, {"symbol": "on", "gloss": "Resting atop.", "nl_synonyms": ["on top of"]}, {"symbol": "under", "gloss": "Beneath.", "nl_synonyms": ["below"]}, {"symbol": "next_to", "gloss": "Adjacent to.", "nl_synonyms": ["beside"]}, {"symbol": "left_of", "gloss": "To the left of.", "nl_synonyms": ["left of"]}, {"symbol": "right_of", "gloss": "To the right of.", "nl_synonyms": ["right of"]}, {"symbol": "in_front_of", "gloss": "Positioned in front of.", "nl_synonyms": ["in front of"]}, {"symbol": "behind", "gloss": "Positioned behind.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Put the bowl right of the spoon.", "braincode": "ACTION place(target=bowl, destination=spoon, relation=right_of)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the missing directional relations required by sampled household placement tasks.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "search-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical values for search, filtering, ranking, currency, genre, category, and availability attributes.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "price", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: monetary cost.", "nl_synonyms": ["cheapest", "lowest price"]}, {"symbol": "rating", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: user or critic score.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "distance", "gloss": "Rank field: proximity.", "nl_synonyms": ["nearest", "closest"]}, {"symbol": "asc", "gloss": "Ascending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["lowest first"]}, {"symbol": "desc", "gloss": "Descending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["highest first"]}, {"symbol": "usd", "gloss": "United States dollar currency.", "nl_synonyms": ["$"]}, {"symbol": "game", "gloss": "Category: video game.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limited_time_offers", "gloss": "Category: time-limited deals.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "in_stock", "gloss": "Available for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["available"]}, {"symbol": "out_of_stock", "gloss": "Unavailable for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["sold out"]}], "membership_rule": "Members belong to one facet: rank-field, rank-direction, currency, genre, category, or availability. rank_field accepts one rank-field symbol or a LIST of them; rank_direction accepts asc or desc. Dedicated search attributes always encode their matching criterion before select_filter or apply_filters may be used.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the cheapest mirror under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, max_price=20, currency=usd) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=price, rank_direction=asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds typed search and ranking vocabulary, including the previously invalid price ranking example.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "role-recipient", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical social or organizational roles used as recipients and audiences. Named individuals remain transitional STRING values during N2's build phase; their future atomic literal form is deferred to N5.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "user", "gloss": "The requesting human.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "agent", "gloss": "The assistant.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "manager", "gloss": "The user's manager.", "nl_synonyms": ["boss"]}, {"symbol": "customer", "gloss": "A customer.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "professor", "gloss": "An instructor.", "nl_synonyms": ["teacher"]}, {"symbol": "support_agent", "gloss": "A customer-support representative.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A lowercase_underscore relationship or institutional role. This category is for roles, not proper names; STRING fallback for named people is retained only through the current N2/N3 build phase and is not a claim about the later closed language.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite email to my manager.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, tone=polite, content=\"follow-up\")"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides an individually look-upable recipient category while explicitly avoiding a false claim that proper names are permanently STRING.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "tone-value", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of canonical tone values used by communication, utterance, and generation attributes.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "formal", "gloss": "Professional and conventional.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "polite", "gloss": "Courteous.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "neutral", "gloss": "Neither warm nor hostile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "urgent", "gloss": "Emphasizes time sensitivity.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "casual", "gloss": "Informal and relaxed.", "nl_synonyms": ["casually"]}, {"symbol": "friendly", "gloss": "Warm and approachable.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "empathetic", "gloss": "Shows understanding of feelings.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "firm", "gloss": "Clear and assertive.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apologetic", "gloss": "Expresses regret.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "persuasive", "gloss": "Intended to convince.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "humorous", "gloss": "Intended to amuse.", "nl_synonyms": ["funny"]}, {"symbol": "supportive", "gloss": "Offers encouragement or help.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Brief and direct.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Provides substantial detail.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite follow-up.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, tone=polite, content=\"follow-up\")"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the real glossary category already required by Action, Utterance, and Generate semantics.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "artifact-specification", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical artifact targets and generation facets for format, style, locale, and duration units.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "story", "gloss": "Artifact: narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "short_text", "gloss": "Artifact: short constrained text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "technical_introduction", "gloss": "Artifact: introductory technical explanation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "contract", "gloss": "Artifact: agreement or contract.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_report", "gloss": "Artifact: headed report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "character_profile", "gloss": "Artifact: fictional character profile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "scene", "gloss": "Artifact: dramatic or narrative scene.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "plan", "gloss": "Artifact: actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bullet_points", "gloss": "Format: bullet list.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_sections", "gloss": "Format: headed sections.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "paragraph", "gloss": "Format: prose paragraph form.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "balanced", "gloss": "Style: presents competing perspectives fairly.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Style: extensive detail.", "nl_synonyms": ["thorough"]}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Style: brief.", "nl_synonyms": ["brief"]}, {"symbol": "en_us", "gloss": "Locale: United States English.", "nl_synonyms": ["English"]}, {"symbol": "day", "gloss": "Duration unit: calendar day.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "hour", "gloss": "Duration unit: hour.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "week", "gloss": "Duration unit: seven-day week.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}], "membership_rule": "Each member belongs to exactly one facet: artifact target, format, style, locale, or duration unit. GENERATE target accepts artifact targets; format/style/locale/duration_unit accept only members of their corresponding facet. duration is meaningful only as the ordered pair duration=NUMBER, duration_unit=<unit>.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write a balanced structured report for a two-week project.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=structured_report, format=structured_sections, style=balanced, duration=2, duration_unit=week, content=\"project report\") -> report : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds the missing artifact-type category and fixes duration by making its unit an explicit glossary value with a normative composition rule.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member\n\nSignatures: search_web(target, [location,distance,min_rating,max_price,currency,genre,category,color,size,shape,availability,audience_class]); search_travel(origin,destination,date,[return_date,passengers]); search_transit(origin,destination,[date,near]); sort(target,rank_field,rank_direction) | legacy sort(target,ordering); extract(target,limit); read_page(target,[content]); pick_up(target,[source]); place(target,destination,[relation,destination_location,destination_relation]); modify_code(target,[module,class,function,call,argument,assertion,reproduction_step,expected_output,actual_output,environment,platform,content]); run_tests(target,[test_id]); send_email/send_message(recipient,content,[tone]); check_replied(target,deadline); check_support_status(target,metric); offer_discount(target,[discount_percent,content]); offer_expedited_shipping(target,[content]); custom_<domain>_<verb>(target,[destination,content]). All other existing normative operations retain exactly their prior listed signatures.", "semantics": "An Action attribute is valid only if it is an attribute-name member and is listed in that operation's signature; unknown or inapplicable attributes are static errors. Category-valued attributes must use the category required by attribute-name. Dedicated search attributes are canonical: a criterion represented by location, rating, price, genre, category, color, size, shape, availability, audience_class, distance, rank_field, or rank_direction must not also appear in select_filter/apply_filters content. select_filter is used for exactly one residual criterion and apply_filters for two or more. Existing result categories, REF/coreference behavior, and all prior listed operation signatures remain unchanged. custom operations use the deterministic operation-vocabulary rule and preserve the prior default fallback's target/destination/content coverage.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the lowest-priced gray round mirror in stock under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, color=gray, shape=round, availability=in_stock, max_price=20, currency=usd) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=price, rank_direction=asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action now validates every attribute against the complete attribute index and an operation-specific signature. Search, household, support, and code operations can therefore use typed vocabulary without allowing arbitrary attribute names.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Replaces generic IDENT=value admission with a normative, machine-checkable attribute and applicability gate while retaining all previously expressible listed and fallback operations.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= \"target\" \"=\" artifact-target | \"quantity\" \"=\" UNSIGNED_INT | \"tone\" \"=\" tone-value | \"format\" \"=\" artifact-format | \"style\" \"=\" artifact-style | \"locale\" \"=\" artifact-locale | \"audience_role\" \"=\" role-recipient | \"audience\" \"=\" STRING | \"duration\" \"=\" NUMBER | \"duration_unit\" \"=\" duration-unit | \"content\" \"=\" STRING | \"exclude\" \"=\" STRING\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only the listed Generate attributes are legal; duplicate, unknown, or inapplicable attributes are static errors. target is required and is an artifact-specification target member. format, style, locale, and duration_unit use their matching artifact-specification facets; tone uses tone-value; audience_role uses role-recipient. duration and duration_unit must occur together and mean exactly that numeric amount in the stated unit. content and exclude remain explicitly transitional STRING channels in this N2/N3 build phase. All prior GENERATE result, REF prohibition, and exact quantity semantics remain unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write ten funny short texts in English.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=short_text, quantity=10, tone=humorous, locale=en_us, content=\"about finding quahogs on a beach\") -> texts : LIST[STRING]"}, "glossary_gloss": "GENERATE now accepts only documented artifact, audience, register, duration, and transitional-content attributes. Duration has an explicit glossary-defined unit instead of an implied one.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies normative Generate applicability, artifact targets, real tone/category references, and N3-compliant duration composition.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary speech-act member\nutter-attr ::= \"content\" \"=\" STRING | \"recipient\" \"=\" (role-recipient | STRING) | \"tone\" \"=\" tone-value | \"register_note\" \"=\" STRING | \"target\" \"=\" STRING | \"audience\" \"=\" STRING", "semantics": "UTTER accepts only the listed attributes, all of which are indexed by attribute-name; unknown attributes are static errors. tone and register_note remain mutually exclusive. content remains a transitional STRING payload during the vocabulary-building phase, and UTTER remains legal only inside a CONVO TURN.", "worked_example": {"nl": "User casually thanks the agent.", "braincode": "CONVO Thanks {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge(content=\"Thanks\", recipient=agent, tone=casual)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance now uses the same complete attribute gate as Actions and generation while preserving conversational prose content during the build phase.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Ensures the claimed attribute index is normatively complete for UTTER as well as Action and Generate.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N2"}]
Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The proposal makes substantial, sound progress on the N2 vocabulary-building direction and preserves current STRING-based coverage as the build phase requires. It cannot be accepted because its central claim of a complete glossary is logically false: structural tokens, retained operation entries, lexical primitives, and several attribute/category definitions are missing, while canonical encoding remains ambiguous. Correcting these concrete inconsistencies would retain the proposal's positive coverage and expressivity gains without requiring premature closure of free-text channels.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "structural-word", "change": "Make the structural inventory actually complete for the current grammar: add AND, OR, NOT, TURN, SPEAKER, USER, AGENT, REPLY_TO, REVISES, DECREASES, CONTEXT, all grammar delimiters and separators (`{}`, `()`, `[]`, `,`, `:`, `=`, `->`), COMMENT, IDENT, UNSIGNED_INT, HEX, and every literal-form name/rule. Define each lexical form precisely, including whitespace and identifier formation."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace the circular membership rule 'all current normative Action registry identifiers' with individually look-upable entries, or a glossary-contained exhaustive registry table, for every retained Action and UTTER operation including click, fill_field, submit, heat, turn_on, add_file, call, propose, acknowledge, and confirm. Give each entry its canonical symbol, signature reference, and synonym mapping."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Define a deterministic NL normalization algorithm for custom operations: domain-selection precedence, tokenization, lemmatization/head-verb selection, multiword verb handling, collision handling, and the rule for when a listed operation overrides custom. Resolve overlapping synonyms, notably `take` currently mapping to both extract and pick_up."}, {"target": "attribute-name and Generate", "change": "Add `exclude` to the complete attribute-name index with value class and Generate applicability. Audit all retained Action, UTTER, Task, and Generate attributes against the index, including legacy operations retained through the registry rule, so the completeness claim and static-validation rule are true."}, {"target": "Action, Generate, and Utterance", "change": "State one canonical attribute order, such as signature order followed by lexical order for optional attributes, and require it in emitted expressions. State canonical ordering for independent sequential generated steps when the NL request does not impose an order."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "change": "Avoid duplicate unqualified symbols with different category meanings: either namespace symbols or define an explicit global disambiguation rule for `detailed` and `concise`, which are members of both tone-value and artifact-specification. Split the entity-descriptor's mixed entity/location/state/position/modifier/platform membership into separately named, independently look-upable facet categories as N2 requires."}, {"target": "worked examples", "change": "Repair invalid or contradictory examples. The structural-word example returns `one` outside the IF child scope that binds it; the operation-vocabulary rinse example relies on entity symbols despite an unresolved target value rule; and the Utterance example uses `acknowledge`, which must be an explicit operation-vocabulary member."}, {"target": "descriptive vocabulary", "change": "Add missing categories, not merely more members, exposed by the simulations: itinerary/day/stop/route and travel-time constraints; transport stop-count and policy/amenity criteria; media venue/showtime/ticket/seat; instrument relation; code file/method/property/call/assertion and expected-versus-actual behavior; revision/improvement intent; procedure/safety/escalation; and academic/job-search goal structures."}, {"target": "Action compatibility", "change": "Reconcile the revised `deadline=ISO_DATE` definition with the existing check_replied semantics and examples requiring a UTC timestamp. Define a glossary literal category for the actual permitted deadline form or explicitly revise the operation semantics without losing current deadline coverage."}]
Logic issues: ["The proposed `structural-word` category calls itself the closed inventory of all structural words but omits many tokens used by the retained grammar, including AND, OR, NOT, TURN, SPEAKER, USER, AGENT, REPLY_TO, REVISES, CONTEXT, DECREASES, delimiters, separators, `->`, IDENT, and COMMENT.", "The operation-vocabulary membership rule delegates coverage to an external 'current normative Action registry' rather than making every operation independently look-upable in the glossary; this does not realize N2 for retained operations.", "The structural-word worked example is statically invalid because `one` is bound inside the IF branch scope and returned outside it.", "The claim that the attribute-name entry is complete is false because Generate permits `exclude` but attribute-name has no exclude member.", "The Action revision leaves emitted attribute ordering unconstrained, producing multiple valid encodings for the same operation.", "The synonym table is not a function: `take` maps to both `extract` and `pick_up`, so it cannot provide N7's required canonical symbol selection.", "The custom-operation rule relies on undefined natural-language notions of source head verb and domain and therefore does not mechanically determine one custom symbol.", "The global symbols `detailed` and `concise` occur in both tone-value and artifact-specification with different meanings, without namespaces or a disambiguation rule.", "The revised deadline attribute conflicts with existing check_replied examples and semantics: it says ISO_DATE, while current valid use requires a full UTC timestamp.", "The stated build-phase retention of STRING is appropriate for N2, but therefore N1, N3, N4, and N5 remain violated; the proposal must not imply that transitional STRING payloads are category-valued descriptive symbols."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The new entity, search, role, artifact, relation, operation, and code-oriented vocabulary gives many held-out task concepts a documented home while retaining STRING channels required by N2's build phase. The custom-operation rule also preserves a broad fallback, but its narrow three-attribute signature still leaves structured concepts such as instruments, seat ranges, and multi-stop itinerary constraints opaque."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The simulations can preserve more distinctions structurally: price ranking, currency, availability, stateful household objects, duration units, artifact kind, tone, and code locations are now available. However, much of the meaning in the travel, code, medical, and revision requests still resides in transitional STRING content, and several requested constraints have no typed attribute or descriptive category."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Typed search fields, state-composition order, duration pairing, and operation-specific validation improve convergence. But attribute order is not canonicalized; `pick_up` and `extract` both claim the synonym \"take\"; listed operations are not individually enumerated or glossed; and `custom_<domain>_<normalized-source-head-verb>` depends on undefined head-verb/domain analysis. The independent flight translations also disagree on bound names, origins, date contexts, quoted versus symbolic ranking values, and filter segmentation."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The categorized entries are a substantial improvement over an operator-only glossary and make many symbols independently understandable. Yet the claimed complete lexicon is contradicted by absent structural tokens, absent operation entries, duplicate symbols with facet-dependent meanings, and undefined lexical rules for identifiers, punctuation, brackets, arrows, and many reserved words."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "A weaker executor benefits from explicit typed filters, rank direction, entity state, spatial relation, recipient role, and artifact facets rather than having to infer all of them from prose. The benefit is limited where strings still carry the operative plan or code change, but retaining those channels is required during this N2 build phase."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "held-trip-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Plan a 3-day itinerary in Kyoto that includes at least one temple per day and avoids anything more than a 20-minute walk from the last stop.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanKyotoItinerary\nTASK PlanKyotoItinerary : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=plan, duration=3, duration_unit=day, content=\"itinerary in Kyoto; at least one temple per day; each next stop at most a 20-minute walk from the preceding stop\") -> itinerary : STRING\n  RETURN itinerary\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "artifact-specification supplies plan and duration units. Per-day quantification and consecutive-stop walking constraints remain prose because no itinerary, stop, route, temporal-unit, or distance/travel-time category exists."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If my manager hasn't replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up; otherwise do nothing.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FollowUpManager\nTASK FollowUpManager CONTEXT execution_date=\"2026-09-30\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=manager, deadline=\"2026-10-02\") -> replied : BOOL\n  IF NOT replied THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, tone=polite, content=\"follow-up\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "role-recipient and tone-value help. The new attribute index says deadline is an ISO_DATE during the build phase, whereas the old Flow-If example requires a UTC instant, leaving an unresolved compatibility issue."}, {"item_id": "8fb78266-8862-4608-9ff3-92f81e58b2ff", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find the cheapest non-stop or 1 stop flight from JFK, New York to Changi, Singapore for 1 traveler on April 11 which includes seat selection and free cancellation", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindCheapestFlight\nTASK FindCheapestFlight CONTEXT execution_date=\"2023-04-05\" : REF[STRING] {\n  ACTION search_travel(origin=\"JFK, New York\", destination=\"Changi, Singapore\", date=\"2023-04-11\", passengers=1) -> flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION apply_filters(target=flights, content=\"non-stop or one stop; seat selection; free cancellation\") -> filtered_flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=filtered_flights, rank_field=price, rank_direction=asc) -> sorted_flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=sorted_flights, limit=1) -> cheapest_flight : REF[STRING]\n  RETURN cheapest_flight\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "search-value materially improves price sorting. Stop count, seat selection, and cancellation policy still have no typed search criteria and remain in the transitional filter payload."}, {"item_id": "29f47ddb-3d25-4cfb-b1d6-d3987e998a13", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Check the movie \"65\" that is digital at the AMC Grove City 14 showing at 7:30 pm on Tuesday, March 28, 2023 and buy four tickets for seats J10 through J7", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BuyMovieTickets\nTASK BuyMovieTickets {\n  ACTION custom_application_buy(target=\"65\", content=\"digital showing at AMC Grove City 14 on 2023-03-28 at 19:30; buy four tickets for seats J10, J9, J8, J7\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The deterministic custom operation preserves the actionable core only as a target/content fallback. There is no category for media format, venue, showtime, ticket, seat, or seat range."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_083350_272263#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Examine a book by the light of a small lamp.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExamineBook\nTASK ExamineBook {\n  ACTION custom_household_examine(target=book, content=\"by the light of a small lamp\")\n  ACTION turn_on(target=\"small_lamp\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The current normative registry retains turn_on and the custom-operation rule admits examine. The required instrument/light relation is still an opaque content string; no instrument attribute exists."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190909_014042_055607#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "rinse a rag off in the sink and put it inside of the tub", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RinseAndPlaceRag\nTASK RinseAndPlaceRag {\n  ACTION rinse(target=rag, destination=sink) -> rag : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=rag, destination=tub, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "spatial-relation provides canonical in/inside. Under N6, rag and tub are assumed members of entity-descriptor, but neither is presently listed."}, {"item_id": "matplotlib__matplotlib-25775", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "[ENH]: Add get/set_antialiased to Text objects\n### Problem\n\nCurrently, Text objects always retrieve their antialiasing state via the global rcParams[\"text.antialias\"], unlike other artists for which this can be configured on a per-artist basis via `set_antialiased` (and read via `set_antialiased`).\n\n### Proposed solution\n\nAdd similar getters/setters on Text objects (also adjusting Annotations accordingly, if needed) and use that info in the drawing stage.\r\n\r\nShould be relatively easy to implement, except that the slight fiddling needed with backends requires some understanding of backend code (I think we need to replace the access to `rcParams[\"text.antialiased\"]` by going through the GraphicsContext state).\n", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddTextAntialiasing\nTASK AddTextAntialiasing {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"Text antialiasing\", module=\"matplotlib.text\", class=\"Text\", content=\"add get_antialiased and set_antialiased; adjust Annotation if needed; use per-artist state in drawing; replace rcParams text antialias access with GraphicsContext state in backend_agg and backend_cairo\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "module and class improve software-location structure, but method names, affected files, calls, expected behavior, and implementation conditions remain prose in content."}, {"item_id": "django__django-16877", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "New template filter `escapeseq`\nDescription\n\t\nFollowing #34574, and after some conversations within the security team, it seems appropriate to provide a new template filter escapeseq which would be to escape what safeseq is to safe. An example of usage would be:\n{{ some_list|escapeseq|join:\",\" }}\nwhere each item of some_list is escaped before applying the join operation. This usage makes sense in a context where autoescape is off.\n", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddEscapeseq\nTASK AddEscapeseq {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"new template filter escapeseq\", module=\"django.template.defaultfilters\", content=\"add escapeseq; escape each member of some_list before join; support use when autoescape is off; analogous to safeseq relative to safe\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "Code module structure is captured, but filter semantics, call composition, argument, and environment are not symbolically modeled."}, {"item_id": "c2734", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "what do you think about the movie her?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovieOpinion\nCONVO MovieOpinion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"what do you think about the movie Her?\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The question speech act and recipient are structured, but its substantive topic/opinion request remains prose. This is retained intentionally in the N2 build phase, although N4 remains unmet."}, {"item_id": "c5739", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "hi, who are you?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT IdentityConversation\nCONVO IdentityConversation {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"hi, who are you?\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation structure, speaker, speech act, and recipient are preserved; identity-question substance stays in STRING."}, {"item_id": "c6577", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "What do you think of video games?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT VideoGameOpinion\nCONVO VideoGameOpinion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"What do you think of video games?\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is an opinion-seeking speech act but its subject and requested judgment are prose payload."}, {"item_id": "c872", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Why are there neurosurgeons who don't like conscious brain surgeries?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT NeurosurgeryQuestion\nCONVO NeurosurgeryQuestion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Why are there neurosurgeons who do not like conscious brain surgeries?\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The explanatory question is represented as UTTER ask, but medical entities and causal content have no descriptive vocabulary."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-10809", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "我写了一篇英语作文，请将它修饰的更好，使用一些高级词汇和高级句式，注重句子之间的衔接和格式。以下是我的作文：Whereas, I prefer to recommend Bup T--the Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications. Seated in Beijing, Bup T has an Outstanding location, Abundant culture resources and a unique International policy background. So There are various opportunities here waiting for you in the coming four years. Additionally, Bu PT is famous for its extraordinary communication engineering, Which is ranked among the top three in the country. ", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ImproveEssay\nTASK ImproveEssay : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, style=detailed, locale=en_us, content=\"improve the supplied English university-recommendation essay using advanced vocabulary and sentence structures; improve cohesion and formatting; source essay: Whereas, I prefer to recommend Bup T--the Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications. Seated in Beijing, Bup T has an Outstanding location, Abundant culture resources and a unique International policy background. So There are various opportunities here waiting for you in the coming four years. Additionally, Bu PT is famous for its extraordinary communication engineering, Which is ranked among the top three in the country.\") -> improved_essay : STRING\n  RETURN improved_essay\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "artifact target, locale, and style are structured, but the source text and revision instructions are prose. `style=detailed` is also ambiguous because detailed is separately a tone-value and artifact style member."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-83611", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "写一篇200字左右的英语作文：疫情期间，你已经上过很多网课，网课有蛮多弊端，有的无法避免，但是还是有改进的余地，就你的体验，比较和分析，你认为老师应该怎么做，学生会更加主动投入到教学活动中？\n文章应包括：1.网课的现状50% 2.你的改进措施50%", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT OnlineClassEssay\nTASK OnlineClassEssay : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, quantity=200, locale=en_us, format=structured_sections, content=\"English essay about online-class drawbacks during the pandemic and teacher measures for student engagement; compare and analyze from experience; approximately half current situation and half improvement measures\") -> essay : STRING\n  RETURN essay\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Quantity, locale, and section format are structurally encoded. Topic, required argument, and fifty/fifty section constraint are opaque content; quantity=200 incorrectly means exactly 200 words rather than the requested approximate length."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-2062", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "Write an intellectual reply to following message: The reason I shared my number was that we could meet", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftReply\nTASK DraftReply : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, tone=formal, content=\"write an intellectual reply to: The reason I shared my number was that we could meet\") -> reply : STRING\n  RETURN reply\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Generation intent and formal register are structured, but intellectual is not a defined tone/style value and the source message remains prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-47203", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0301)", "nl": "please draft it in a legal way ", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftLegalClause\nTASK DraftLegalClause : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=contract, tone=formal, content=\"draft the supplied material as a legal clause\") -> clause : STRING\n  RETURN clause\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "contract and formal tone help, but legal register is not a glossary value and the referent \"it\" requires prior conversational material not supplied in this isolated item."}, {"item_id": "1776049257672", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "How to perform cpr on my dog?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DogCPRGuidance\nTASK DogCPRGuidance : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, format=structured_sections, content=\"give concise emergency guidance for performing CPR on a dog, including urgent veterinary-care escalation\") -> guidance : STRING\n  RETURN guidance\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested structured guidance format is represented, but CPR procedure, dog entity, emergency conditions, safety constraints, and escalation semantics are all prose."}, {"item_id": "1776008565711", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "i need help wrinting a paper for university", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT UniversityPaperHelp\nCONVO UniversityPaperHelp {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"I need help writing a paper for university.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "This is correctly modeled as a conversational help request, but academic-paper type, help stage, and constraints are absent from the vocabulary."}, {"item_id": "1775947518795", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "tell me 3 options for travels to beach destinies in april", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BeachTravelOptions\nTASK BeachTravelOptions : LIST[STRING] {\n  GENERATE(target=plan, quantity=3, format=structured_sections, content=\"three April beach-travel destination options\") -> options : LIST[STRING]\n  RETURN options\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Exact count and output organization are structured, but beach destination, April, travel suitability, and option criteria remain in content."}, {"item_id": "1775967991797", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "I need help finding a job, or at least letting one come to me", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT JobSearchHelp\nCONVO JobSearchHelp {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"I need help finding a job, or at least letting one come to me.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational request is preserved, but job-search goals, active/passive strategy alternatives, and the user's constraints have no symbolic representation."}]
Rebuttal rulings on your previous rebuttals (if any): []
Address every required change — either comply, or put it in `rebuttals` with a concrete argument (evidence from the simulated items, a conflict with another construct or with a fundamental note) for why it should not be made. The Critic rules on each rebuttal; an overruled rebuttal must be complied with next time. Never rebut a change that enforces a `hard` fundamental note. Revising an existing spec construct is `op: "revise"` with the same construct_name.

Return JSON: {"summary": "1-2 sentences on what this set of changes achieves", "note_position": "comply" | "contest", "note_argument": "how the changes realize the note, or the evidence for contesting it", "foundations_overview": "..." | null, "changes": [{"op": "add" | "revise" | "remove", "construct_name": "...", "grammar": "...", "semantics": "...", "worked_example": {"nl": "...", "braincode": "..."}, "glossary_gloss": "...", "change_type": "MAJOR" | "MINOR" | "PATCH", "rationale": "...", "cites_source": "..." | null, "addresses_note": "N<k>" | null} — or, for a category of the descriptive lexicon (actions, objects, roles, attribute values, literal forms): {"op": "add" | "revise" | "remove", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "<category name, e.g. tone-value>", "glossary_gloss": "...", "closed": true | false, "members": [{"symbol": "...", "gloss": "...", "nl_synonyms": ["..."]}], "membership_rule": "..." | null, "worked_example": {"nl": "...", "braincode": "..."}, "change_type": "MAJOR" | "MINOR" | "PATCH", "rationale": "...", "addresses_note": "N<k>" | null}, ...], "rebuttals": [{"target": "...", "change": "<the required change you contest>", "argument": "..."}, ...]}

