   "membership_rule": "Custom operations are formed as `custom_<domain>_<verb>`. Domain is the first match in {web, household, code, communication, filesystem, application, support} applicable to the target. Verb is the lemmatized, lowercase, underscore-joined head verb of the source action. If the verb matches a listed operation's synonym, the listed operation must be used. Synonyms are mutually exclusive functions.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Examine a book.",
    "braincode": "ACTION custom_household_examine(target=\"book\", content=\"examine\")"
   },
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "Replaces the circular rule with an exhaustive list of all retained operations and a deterministic custom operation algorithm.",
