ose an order."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "change": "Avoid duplicate unqualified symbols with different category meanings: either namespace symbols or define an explicit global disambiguation rule for `detailed` and `concise`, which are members of both tone-value and artifact-specification. Split the entity-descriptor's mixed entity/location/state/position/modifier/platform membership into separately named, independently look-upable facet categories as N2 requires."}, {"target": "worked examples", "change": "Repair invalid or contradictory examples. The structural-word example returns `one` outside the IF child scope that binds it; the operation-vocabulary rinse example relies on entity symbols despite an unresolved target value rule; and the Utterance example uses `acknowledge`, which must be an explicit operation-vocabulary member."}, {"target": "descriptive vocabulary", "change": "Add missing categories, not merely more members, exposed by the simulations: itinerary/day/stop/route and travel-time constraints; transport stop-count and policy/amenity criteria; media venue/showtime/ticket/seat; instrument relation; code file/method/property/call/assertion and expected-versus-actual behavior; revision/improvement intent; procedure/safety/escalation; and academic/job-search goal structures."}, {"target": "Action compatibility", "change": "Reconcile the revised `deadline=ISO_DATE` definition with the existing check_replied semantics and examples requiring a UTC timestamp. Define a glossary literal category for the actual permitted deadline form or explicitly revise the operation semantics without losing current deadline coverage."}]
