ti-step preparation or one custom operation, software-fix target and evidence fields, and even whether recipe/persona requests are expressible. The new ordering rules do not resolve these construct-selection and decomposition differences."}, "required_changes": [{"target": "structural-word", "change": "Make the claimed complete structural lexicon actually cover the retained grammar: add or precisely define NUMBER's signed/decimal/exponent form, STRING escaping, diff's '-' token, ISO_DATE, COMMENT as a named lexical category, reserved-word exclusion from IDENT, and every punctuation/operator token used by all retained productions. Correct the worked example so it is a valid demonstration of its stated condition semantics rather than an unused IF."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace the custom-operation heuristic with a fully executable canonicalization procedure: ordered domain precedence, source tokenization, multiword-verb handling, lemmatizer/reference rule, head selection, collision handling, and explicit fallback for no domain match. State signatures/result categories for every retained operation rather than relying on 'other operations retain prior signatures.'"}, {"target": "attribute-name and value categories", "change": "For every indexed attribute, state its permitted value category or literal form and make Action's grammar enforce it per operation signature. In particular define categories/rules for target, destination, source, destination_location, destination_relation, audience, module, class, function, call, argument, assertion, reproduction_step, expected_output, actual_output, environment, platform, and instrument; a bare generic value production does not satisfy N3."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "change": "Complete the promised facet split by adding independently look-upable entity-state, entity-modifier, position, platform-name, and location categories, with exact membership rules and synonym mappings