osition, custom-domain selection, and many synonym/value mappings remain underdefined, as the independent translations demonstrate."}, "N1": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "The build phase correctly retains STRING and free identifiers, so closure is not expected yet. The added glossary vocabulary helps eventual closure but does not make every simulated token glossary-traceable."}, "N4": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "The proposal intentionally preserves STRING content in the N2 build phase, as required. It neither removes prose nor should it do so before the vocabulary can replace it."}, "N5": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Precise lexical rules and named vocabularies improve self-containment, but generic lowercase_underscore entities, incomplete literal rules, and undefined normalization behavior still require unstated English/source-language judgment."}, "N6": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Several productions now reference vocabulary facets rather than only currently listed words. Missing categories, especially for travel, food, medical, procedures, academic tasks, and rich software concepts, still force content prose instead of category-shaped expressions."}, "N8": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "The additions preserve useful distinctions for price, availability, spatial relation, code behavior, roles, tone, and artifacts. Richness remains substantially constrained by missing domain categories and by opaque content fields for compatibility, procedures, and detailed requirements."}}, "rebuttal_rulings": [{"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "ruling": "overruled", "reasoning": "Narrowing entity-name removes some prior mixing, but it does not create the separately named state, modifier, position, and platform categories explicitly required for a complete N2 lexicon. The sprint limit explains deferral but does not establish that the required change is unnecessary."}, {"target": "descriptive vocabulary", "ruling": "overruled", "reasoning": "The change limit may justify staging, but it does not answer the substantive coverage and lexicon gaps exposed by the simulations. These missing categories must remain required for subsequent N2 realization; the proposal must not characterize its present vocabulary as exhaustive or complete."}], "accept_changes": [], "chosen_position": null, "position_comparison": null, "reasoning": "The bundle makes meaningful N2 progress by adding genuine vocabulary categories and useful canonical ordering, while preserving the required transitional STRING channels. It cannot be accepted because it claims exhaustive completeness while leaving lexical rules, value typing, domain categories, and custom-operation normalization materially underspecified. These defects undermine the proposed determinism and interpretability gains, though the overall direction is sound and should be reworked rather than rejected."}
