eb(target=\"mirror\", currency=usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=price, rank_direction=asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds typed search and ranking vocabulary.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "role-recipient", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical social or organizational roles used as recipients and audiences.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "user", "gloss": "The requesting human.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "agent", "gloss": "The assistant.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "manager", "gloss": "The user's manager.", "nl_synonyms": ["boss"]}, {"symbol": "customer", "gloss": "A customer.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "professor", "gloss": "An instructor.", "nl_synonyms": ["teacher"]}, {"symbol": "support_agent", "gloss": "A customer-support representative.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A lowercase_underscore relationship or institutional role.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite email to my manager.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, content=\"follow-up\", tone=polite)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides an individually look-upable recipient category.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "tone-value", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of canonical tone values used by communication, utterance, and generation attributes.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "formal", "gloss": "Professional and conventional.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "polite", "gloss": "Courteous.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "neutral", "gloss": "Neither warm nor hostile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "urgent", "gloss": "Emphasizes time sensitivity.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "casual", "gloss": "Informal and relaxed.", "nl_synonyms": ["casually"]}, {"symbol": "friendly", "gloss": "Warm and approachable.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "empathetic", "gloss": "Shows understanding of feelings.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "firm", "gloss": "Clear and assertive.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apologetic", "gloss": "Expresses regret.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "persuasive", "gloss": "Intended to convince.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "humorous", "gloss": "Intended to amuse.", "nl_synonyms": ["funny"]}, {"symbol": "supportive", "gloss": "Offers encouragement or help.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Brief tone.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Detailed tone.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "When a symbol (e.g., detailed, concise) exists in multiple categories, it is resolved by the expected category of the attribute it binds to.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite follow-up.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, content=\"follow-up\", tone=polite)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the real glossary category already required by Action, Utterance, and Generate semantics, with a global disambiguation rule.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "artifact-specification", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical artifact targets and generation facets for format, style, locale, and duration units.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "story", "gloss": "Artifact: narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "short_text", "gloss": "Artifact: short constrained text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "technical_introduction", "gloss": "Artifact: introductory technical explanation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "contract", "gloss": "Artifact: agreement or contract.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_report", "gloss": "Artifact: headed report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "character_profile", "gloss": "Artifact: fictional character profile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "scene", "gloss": "Artifact: dramatic or narrative scene.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "plan", "gloss": "Artifact: actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bullet_points", "gloss": "Format: bullet list.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_sections", "gloss": "Format: headed sections.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "paragraph", "gloss": "Format: prose paragraph form.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "balanced", "gloss": "Style: presents competing perspectives fairly.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Style: extensive detail.", "nl_synonyms": ["thorough"]}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Style: brief.", "nl_synonyms": ["brief"]}, {"symbol": "en_us", "gloss": "Locale: United States English.", "nl_synonyms": ["English"]}, {"symbol": "day", "gloss": "Duration unit: calendar day.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "hour", "gloss": "Duration unit: hour.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "week", "gloss": "Duration unit: seven-day week.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}], "membership_rule": "Each member belongs to exactly one facet: artifact target, format, style, locale, or duration unit. When a symbol (e.g., detailed) exists in multiple categories, it is resolved by the attribute's expected category.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write a balanced structured report for a two-week project.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=structured_report, content=\"project report\", duration=2, duration_unit=week, format=structured_sections, style=balanced) -> report : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds the missing artifact-type category and fixes duration by making its unit an explicit glossary value.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member\n\nSignatures: search_web(target, [audience_class,availability,category,color,currency,distance,genre,location,max_price,min_rating,shape,size]); search_travel(origin,destination,date,[passengers,return_date]); search_transit(origin,destination,[date,near]); sort(target,rank_field,rank_direction) | legacy sort(target,ordering); extract(target,limit); read_page(target,[content]); pick_up(target,[source]); place(target,destination,[destination_location,destination_relation,relation]); modify_code(target,[actual_output,argument,assertion,call,class,content,environment,expected_output,function,module,platform,reproduction_step]); run_tests(target,[test_id]); send_email/send_message(recipient,content,[tone]); check_replied(target,deadline); check_support_status(target,metric); offer_discount(target,[content,discount_percent]); offer_expedited_shipping(target,[content]); custom_<domain>_<verb>(target,[content,destination,instrument]). Other operations retain their prior signatures.", "semantics": "An Action attribute is valid only if it is an attribute-name member and is listed in that operation's signature. Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order, followed by any optional attributes in alphabetical order. When the source text does not impose a sequential order for independent steps, they must be emitted in alphabetical order of their operations, breaking ties by target. Category-valued attributes must use the category required by attribute-name. Dedicated search attributes are canonical: a criterion represented by a dedicated attribute must not also appear in select_filter/apply_filters content. Existing result categories, REF/coreference behavior, and all prior listed operation signatures remain unchanged. Custom operations use the deterministic operation-vocabulary rule.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the lowest-priced mirror in stock under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=\"mirror\", availability=in_stock, currency=usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=price, rank_direction=asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action now validates every attribute against the complete attribute index and an operation-specific signature, enforcing a canonical attribute order.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Enforces a canonical attribute order and exhaustive attribute validation.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= \"target\" \"=\" artifact-target | \"audience\" \"=\" STRING | \"audience_role\" \"=\" role-recipient | \"content\" \"=\" STRING | \"duration\" \"=\" NUMBER | \"duration_unit\" \"=\" duration-unit | \"exclude\" \"=\" STRING | \"format\" \"=\" artifact-format | \"locale\" \"=\" artifact-locale | \"quantity\" \"=\" UNSIGNED_INT | \"style\" \"=\" artifact-style | \"tone\" \"=\" tone-value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only the listed Generate attributes are legal. Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (target, then optional attributes in alphabetical order). Independent sequential generated steps without a source-imposed order must be emitted in alphabetical order of their target values. target is required and is an artifact-specification target member. format, style, locale, and duration_unit use their matching artifact-specification facets; tone uses tone-value; audience_role uses role-recipient. duration and duration_unit must occur together. content and exclude remain transitional STRING channels. All prior GENERATE result, REF prohibition, and exact quantity semantics remain unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write ten funny short texts in English.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=short_text, content=\"about finding quahogs on a beach\", locale=en_us, quantity=10, tone=humorous) -> texts : LIST[STRING]"}, "glossary_gloss": "GENERATE now accepts only documented artifact, audience, register, duration, exclude, and transitional-content attributes, enforcing canonical attribute order.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies normative Generate applicability, canonical ordering, and exclude attribute.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary speech-act member\nutter-attr ::= \"audience\" \"=\" STRING | \"content\" \"=\" STRING | \"recipient\" \"=\" (role-recipient | STRING) | \"register_note\" \"=\" STRING | \"target\" \"=\" STRING | \"tone\" \"=\" tone-value", "semantics": "UTTER accepts only the listed attributes, all of which are indexed by attribute-name. Attributes must be emitted in alphabetical order. Independent sequential UTTER steps without a source-imposed order must be emitted in alphabetical order of their speech acts. tone and register_note remain mutually exclusive. content remains a transitional STRING payload during the vocabulary-building phase, and UTTER remains legal only inside a CONVO TURN.", "worked_example": {"nl": "User casually thanks the agent.", "braincode": "CONVO Thanks {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge(content=\"Thanks\", recipient=agent, tone=casual)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance now uses the complete attribute gate and enforces canonical attribute ordering, preserving conversational prose content during the build phase.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Ensures the claimed attribute index is normatively complete for UTTER and enforces canonical ordering.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N2"}]
Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The bundle makes meaningful N2 progress by adding genuine vocabulary categories and useful canonical ordering, while preserving the required transitional STRING channels. It cannot be accepted because it claims exhaustive completeness while leaving lexical rules, value typing, domain categories, and custom-operation normalization materially underspecified. These defects undermine the proposed determinism and interpretability gains, though the overall direction is sound and should be reworked rather than rejected.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "structural-word", "change": "Make the claimed complete structural lexicon actually cover the retained grammar: add or precisely define NUMBER's signed/decimal/exponent form, STRING escaping, diff's '-' token, ISO_DATE, COMMENT as a named lexical category, reserved-word exclusion from IDENT, and every punctuation/operator token used by all retained productions. Correct the worked example so it is a valid demonstration of its stated condition semantics rather than an unused IF."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace the custom-operation heuristic with a fully executable canonicalization procedure: ordered domain precedence, source tokenization, multiword-verb handling, lemmatizer/reference rule, head selection, collision handling, and explicit fallback for no domain match. State signatures/result categories for every retained operation rather than relying on 'other operations retain prior signatures.'"}, {"target": "attribute-name and value categories", "change": "For every indexed attribute, state its permitted value category or literal form and make Action's grammar enforce it per operation signature. In particular define categories/rules for target, destination, source, destination_location, destination_relation, audience, module, class, function, call, argument, assertion, reproduction_step, expected_output, actual_output, environment, platform, and instrument; a bare generic value production does not satisfy N3."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "change": "Complete the promised facet split by adding independently look-upable entity-state, entity-modifier, position, platform-name, and location categories, with exact membership rules and synonym mappings. Restrict entity-name so its open membership rule cannot be confused with unrestricted IDENT formation."}, {"target": "descriptive vocabulary", "change": "Add the deferred missing categories identified by the simulations: itinerary/day/stop/route and travel-time; transit stop-count and policy/amenity; media venue/showtime/ticket/seat; typed compatibility/instrument relations; code file/method/property/call/assertion and expected-versus-actual behavior; revision/improvement; procedure/safety/escalation; academic/job-search goals; food/nutrition/meal structures; medical topic/audience constraints; and email/message/collaboration structures."}, {"target": "Action, Generate, and Utterance", "change": "Reconcile canonical ordering language into one unambiguous rule for required and optional attributes, define canonical binding/handle naming including numeric suffixes and plural collection names, and ensure every worked example obeys the grammar and the declared value categories."}, {"target": "search-value", "change": "Split search-value into separately named rank-field, rank-direction, currency, genre, category, and availability categories, or give globally unique namespaced symbols. Its current mixed membership is not individually look-upable by the facet that Action signatures require."}]
Logic issues: ["The structural-word category claims a closed complete inventory but omits lexical definitions required by the retained grammar, notably the full NUMBER and STRING forms, ISO_DATE, the diff '-' token, and reserved-word interaction with IDENT.", "The operation-vocabulary custom-operation rule is not deterministic: applicability and domain precedence are undefined, and source-language lemmatization/head-verb selection is delegated to undefined linguistic judgment.", "Action says category-valued attributes must use the category required by attribute-name, but attribute-name does not specify such categories; its grammar accepts generic value for every attribute, making static value validation impossible.", "search-value combines six semantically distinct facets in one vocabulary while Action signatures require facet-specific values; membership is not individually look-upable as N2 requires.", "entity-name's rule 'a generic entity or location is lowercase_underscore' overlaps the IDENT lexical rule and does not give a translator a deterministic boundary between an entity symbol and an arbitrary identifier.", "The structural-word worked example does not demonstrate its NL conditional: it tests TRUE, binds an unused two, and returns one regardless. It cannot validate the claimed structural semantics.", "The proposed operation-vocabulary example uses target=\"book\" and content=\"examine\" while the new prose says category-valued fields must use category members, yet no target/content value class permits or explains the quoted forms."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The proposal materially improves coverage for household relations, search price/rating/category criteria, artifact targets, roles, and code-fix fields. However, it still lacks required descriptive categories for travel structure, transport constraints, media booking, procedure/safety, academic/job-search structures, and several code entities; its restrictive revised signatures also leave some retained operations governed only by an unspecified prior-signature fallback."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The simulations can now represent price ceilings, stock status, ordering, directional placement, recipient roles, output expectations, and several generation constraints structurally rather than placing all of them in content. Compatibility, detailed software reproduction context, entity states/positions, and many domain constraints still require opaque STRING payloads or have no appropriate category."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical attribute ordering and dedicated search fields are useful improvements. But the custom-operation rule is not operationally deterministic: 'first match applicable to the target,' source-language head-verb selection, lemmatization, multiword verbs, and domain selection are not fully defined; the supplied translations still diverge sharply on decomposition, names, compatibility filtering, and software-fix representation."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Individually look-upable vocabulary categories make many symbols clearer than the prior construct-only glossary. The claimed complete inventory is nevertheless false: NUMBER and STRING lexical syntax are not fully specified here, '-' and other tokens used by current grammar are absent, several structural and descriptive value classes are only implicit, and entity-name's generic lowercase_underscore rule is indistinguishable from unrestricted IDENT formation."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "A weaker planner benefits from typed-looking search constraints, named code fields, explicit spatial relations, tone values, and artifact specifications. The benefit is limited where requirements remain buried in content strings, such as compatibility, a bug's reproduction program, or an open-ended generation brief."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=\"pillow\", source=\"sofa\") -> pillow : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow, destination=\"armchair\", relation=on)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=\"pillow\", source=\"sofa\") -> pillow2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow2, destination=\"armchair\", relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The revised pick_up/place signatures and spatial-relation category help. Sequential duplication represents 'one at a time'; no quantity category is needed for this finite two-item request."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If my manager hasn't replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up; otherwise do nothing.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FollowUp\nTASK FollowUp CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=\"manager\", deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL\n  IF NOT replied THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, content=\"follow-up\", tone=polite)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "role-recipient, tone-value, and the corrected UTC_TIMESTAMP deadline improve the representation. The follow-up's substantive wording remains deliberately available through transitional content."}, {"item_id": "e344b89e-767a-4618-ba82-4b81cdcba280", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "add a motherboard under $200 and a compatible processor at any price to the shopping cart.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddParts\nTASK AddParts {\n  ACTION search_web(target=\"motherboard\", currency=usd, max_price=200) -> motherboards : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=motherboards, limit=1) -> motherboard : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(target=motherboard)\n  ACTION search_web(target=\"processor\") -> processors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION select_filter(target=processors, content=\"compatible with motherboard\") -> compatible_processors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=compatible_processors, limit=1) -> processor : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(target=processor)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "search-value improves the price constraint. Compatibility still has no typed relation/category and remains a STRING filtering criterion."}, {"item_id": "f118238f-ef8f-4b63-9159-a81e981ef46e", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Add decorative LED Candles to the cart.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AddCandles\nTASK AddCandles {\n  ACTION search_web(target=\"decorative_led_candles\") -> candles : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=candles, limit=1) -> candles : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION add_to_cart(target=candles)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The current transitional STRING channel still carries the product entity descriptor. No new proposed category materially helps beyond operation indexing."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_214148_552057#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "get a cup ready for coffee", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PrepareCup\nTASK PrepareCup {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=\"cup\", source=\"refrigerator\") -> cup : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=cup, destination=\"microwave\") -> cup : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=cup, destination=\"coffee_maker\", relation=under)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "operation-vocabulary and spatial-relation help. The exact machine cycle completion implied by 'when it is done' is not represented as a condition, but the requested end state and main trajectory are retained."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_102045_139402#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "To put the toilet paper away.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT StoreToiletPaper\nTASK StoreToiletPaper {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=\"toilet_paper\", source=\"toilet\") -> toilet_paper : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=toilet_paper, destination=\"holder\", destination_location=\"wall\", destination_relation=on, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The added nested destination attributes and spatial relation capture the holder-on-wall placement, although their expected value categories are not specified."}, {"item_id": "sympy__sympy-15345", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "mathematica_code gives wrong output with Max: mathematica_code(Max(x,2)) should produce Max[x,2] rather than Max(2, x).", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixMathematicaCode\nTASK FixMathematicaCode {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"sympy_printing_mathematica\", function=\"mathematica_code\", call=\"mathematica_code(Max(x,2))\", expected_output=\"Max[x,2]\", actual_output=\"Max(2, x)\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code attributes improve structure substantially. File/module identity and the actual code change remain in a free identifier/string channel; no file or method category is defined."}, {"item_id": "django__django-15098", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Fix Django internationalisation so i18n_patterns supports locales containing both script and region, including en-Latn-US.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixLocalePattern\nTASK FixLocalePattern {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"django_utils_translation_trans_real\", module=\"django.utils.translation.trans_real\", reproduction_step=\"i18n_patterns rejects en-latn-us and en-Latn-US\", expected_output=\"locale tags with script and region return 200\", actual_output=\"script-and-region locale routes return 404\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The revised modify_code signature supplies useful expected/actual/reproduction slots. The locale grammar, source files, test setup, and required parser behavior remain prose because required code-structure and semantic categories 