      "membership_rule": "An entity or location symbol must be a singular, lowercase_underscore noun phrase representing the physical or conceptual object. It must not contain verbs, states, or modifiers. If it appears in the source, it must be extracted as the head noun phrase. This category is distinct from unrestricted IDENTs which are used for variables and handles.",
      "worked_example": {
        "nl": "Rinse a rag off in the sink and put it inside of the tub.",
        "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=\"rag\") -> rag : REF[STRING]\nACTION rinse(target=rag, destination=\"sink\") -> rinsed_rag : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=rinsed_rag, destination=\"tub\", relation=in)"
      },
      "change_type": "MAJOR",
      "rationale": "Provides base entity nouns. Membership rule restricted to singular head noun phrases to avoid overlap with unrestricted IDENTs.",
      "addresses_note": "N2"
    },
