   "membership_rule": "Custom operations: tokenization splits on whitespace. If the source verb matches a listed synonym, use the listed operation. Otherwise, the custom operation is `custom_<domain>_<verb>`. Domain precedence: web, household, code, communication, filesystem, application, support, unknown. Select the first domain conceptually fitting the target. Verb is the lemmatized (WordNet base form), lowercase, underscore-joined head verb (e.g., 'set up' -> 'set_up'). Collision handling: if two distinct actions yield the same `custom_` name, append `_2` to the second in source order. Fallback domain is `unknown`.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Examine a book.",
    "braincode": "ACTION custom_household_examine(target=\"book\", content=\"examine\")"
   },
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "Replaces the heuristic with a fully executable canonicalization procedure (domain precedence, lemmatization, multiword, collision, fallback).",
   "addresses_note": "N2"
  },
