   "membership_rule": "Value rules: `tone` uses `tone-value`. `format`, `style`, `locale`, `duration_unit` use `artifact-specification`. `currency`, `genre`, `category`, `availability`, `rank_field`, `rank_direction` use `search-value`. `relation`, `destination_relation` use `spatial-relation`. `recipient`, `audience_role` use `role-recipient`. `target`, `destination`, `source`, `instrument` use a bound REF, an `entity-name` member, or a transitional STRING if no member applies. Code identifiers (`module`, `class`, `function`, `call`, `argument`, `assertion`, `test_id`) use a STRING literal matching the exact identifier. `expected_output`, `actual_output`, `reproduction_step`, `environment`, `platform`, `content`, `exclude`, `register_note`, `audience` remain transitional STRING payloads until further categories are added. Numeric fields use NUMBER. Dates use STRING matching ISO_DATE or UTC_TIMESTAMP.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Search flights from Tel Aviv to Berlin next Tuesday for two passengers.",
