Your previous critique's required changes: [{"target": "structural-word", "change": "Make the claimed complete structural lexicon actually cover the retained grammar: add or precisely define NUMBER's signed/decimal/exponent form, STRING escaping, diff's '-' token, ISO_DATE, COMMENT as a named lexical category, reserved-word exclusion from IDENT, and every punctuation/operator token used by all retained productions. Correct the worked example so it is a valid demonstration of its stated condition semantics rather than an unused IF."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace the custom-operation heuristic with a fully executable canonicalization procedure: ordered domain precedence, source tokenization, multiword-verb handling, lemmatizer/reference rule, head selection, collision handling, and explicit fallback for no domain match. State signatures/result categories for every retained operation rather than relying on 'other operations retain prior signatures.'"}, {"target": "attribute-name and value categories", "change": "For every indexed attribute, state its permitted value category or literal form and make Action's grammar enforce it per operation signature. In particular define categories/rules for target, destination, source, destination_location, destination_relation, audience, module, class, function, call, argument, assertion, reproduction_step, expected_output, actual_output, environment, platform, and instrument; a bare generic value production does not satisfy N3."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "change": "Complete the promised facet split by adding independently look-upable entity-state, entity-modifier, position, platform-name, and location categories, with exact membership rules and synonym mappings. Restrict entity-name so its open membership rule cannot be confused with unrestricted IDENT formation."}, {"target": "descriptive vocabulary", "change": "Add the deferred missing categories identified by the simulations: itinerary/day/stop/route and travel-time; transit stop-count and policy/amenity; media venue/showtime/ticket/seat; typed compatibility/instrument relations; code file/method/property/call/assertion and expected-versus-actual behavior; revision/improvement; procedure/safety/escalation; academic/job-search goals; food/nutrition/meal structures; medical topic/audience constraints; and email/message/collaboration structures."}, {"target": "Action, Generate, and Utterance", "change": "Reconcile canonical ordering language into one unambiguous rule for required and optional attributes, define canonical binding/handle naming including numeric suffixes and plural collection names, and ensure every worked example obeys the grammar and the declared value categories."}, {"target": "search-value", "change": "Split search-value into separately named rank-field, rank-direction, currency, genre, category, and availability categories, or give globally unique namespaced symbols. Its current mixed membership is not individually look-upable by the facet that Action signatures require."}]
The Shaper REBUTS some of them instead of complying — rule on each in `rebuttal_rulings` (upheld = the change is dropped; overruled = still required):
