", "gloss": "Ask a question.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "inform", "gloss": "State information.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "respond", "gloss": "Answer.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "propose", "gloss": "Propose an idea.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "correct", "gloss": "Correct a statement.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "acknowledge", "gloss": "Acknowledge.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "confirm", "gloss": "Confirm.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "decline", "gloss": "Decline.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Custom operations: tokenization splits on whitespace. If the source verb matches a listed synonym, use the listed operation. Otherwise, the custom operation is `custom_<domain>_<verb>`. Domain precedence: web, household, code, communication, filesystem, application, support, unknown. Select the first domain conceptually fitting the target. Verb is the lemmatized (WordNet base form), lowercase, underscore-joined head verb (e.g., 'set up' -> 'set_up'). Collision handling: if two distinct actions yield the same `custom_` name, append `_2` to the second in source order. Fallback domain is `unknown`.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Examine a book.", "braincode": "ACTION custom_household_examine(target=\"book\", content=\"examine\")"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Replaces the heuristic with a fully executable canonicalization procedure (domain precedence, lemmatization, multiword, collision, fallback).", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "The initial index of attributes mapping each to its permitted value category or literal rule.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Subject/artifact.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Spatial relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination_location", "gloss": "Nested anchor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination_relation", "gloss": "Relation to anchor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "Transitional payload.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Recipient.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Named reader.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience_role", "gloss": "Reader role.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Register.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "register_note", "gloss": "Transitional register.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Artifact format.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Artifact style.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Artifact locale.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Exact count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Numeric duration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "execution_date", "gloss": "TASK context anchor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Travel date.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "return_date", "gloss": "Travel return.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "passengers", "gloss": "Passenger count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "near", "gloss": "Transit near.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Search location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "distance", "gloss": "Search distance.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "min_rating", "gloss": "Minimum rating.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_price", "gloss": "Maximum price.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "currency", "gloss": "Price currency.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "genre", "gloss": "Search genre.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "category", "gloss": "Search category.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color", "gloss": "Search color.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size", "gloss": "Search size.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "shape", "gloss": "Search shape.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "availability", "gloss": "Search stock.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience_class", "gloss": "Search demographic.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_field", "gloss": "Sort field.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_direction", "gloss": "Sort direction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ordering", "gloss": "Legacy sort order.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limit", "gloss": "Extract member count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Reply deadline.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Support metric.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "discount_percent", "gloss": "Discount percentage.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "module", "gloss": "Code module.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "class", "gloss": "Code class.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "function", "gloss": "Code function.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code call.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "argument", "gloss": "Code argument.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Code assertion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Bug reproduction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Observed behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "environment", "gloss": "Runtime environment.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "test_id", "gloss": "Test identifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "exclude", "gloss": "Generation exclusion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "instrument", "gloss": "Action instrument.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Value rules: `tone` uses `tone-value`. `format`, `style`, `locale`, `duration_unit` use `artifact-specification`. `currency`, `genre`, `category`, `availability`, `rank_field`, `rank_direction` use `search-value`. `relation`, `destination_relation` use `spatial-relation`. `recipient`, `audience_role` use `role-recipient`. `target`, `destination`, `source`, `instrument` use a bound REF, an `entity-name` member, or a transitional STRING if no member applies. Code identifiers (`module`, `class`, `function`, `call`, `argument`, `assertion`, `test_id`) use a STRING literal matching the exact identifier. `expected_output`, `actual_output`, `reproduction_step`, `environment`, `platform`, `content`, `exclude`, `register_note`, `audience` remain transitional STRING payloads until further categories are added. Numeric fields use NUMBER. Dates use STRING matching ISO_DATE or UTC_TIMESTAMP.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Search flights from Tel Aviv to Berlin next Tuesday for two passengers.", "braincode": "ACTION search_travel(origin=\"Tel Aviv\", destination=\"Berlin\", date=\"2025-06-10\", passengers=2) -> flights : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Audited index of attributes, explicitly defining permitted value categories for each to satisfy N3.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "entity-name", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical entity and location base nouns.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mug", "gloss": "Drinking cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rag", "gloss": "Cleaning cloth.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tub", "gloss": "Bathtub.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "book", "gloss": "Reading material.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mirror", "gloss": "Reflective item.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sink", "gloss": "Washing basin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "counter", "gloss": "Countertop surface.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cupboard", "gloss": "Storage cabinet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "refrigerator", "gloss": "Cooling appliance.", "nl_synonyms": ["fridge"]}, {"symbol": "spoon", "gloss": "Eating utensil.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bowl", "gloss": "A bowl.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "pillow", "gloss": "A cushion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sofa", "gloss": "A couch.", "nl_synonyms": ["couch"]}, {"symbol": "armchair", "gloss": "A chair with armrests.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet_paper", "gloss": "Toilet paper.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "holder", "gloss": "A holder.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "wall", "gloss": "A wall.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "motherboard", "gloss": "Computer motherboard.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "processor", "gloss": "Computer processor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "decorative_led_candles", "gloss": "LED candles.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cup", "gloss": "A cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "coffee_maker", "gloss": "Coffee machine.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "microwave", "gloss": "Microwave oven.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet", "gloss": "A toilet.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An entity or location symbol must be a singular, lowercase_underscore noun phrase representing the physical or conceptual object. It must not contain verbs, states, or modifiers. If it appears in the source, it must be extracted as the head noun phrase. This category is distinct from unrestricted IDENTs which are used for variables and handles.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Rinse a rag off in the sink and put it inside of the tub.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=\"rag\") -> rag : REF[STRING]\nACTION rinse(target=rag, destination=\"sink\") -> rinsed_rag : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=rinsed_rag, destination=\"tub\", relation=in)"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Provides base entity nouns. Membership rule restricted to singular head noun phrases to avoid overlap with unrestricted IDENTs.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "spatial-relation", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of relations used when placing one entity relative to another.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "in", "gloss": "Contained within.", "nl_synonyms": ["inside"]}, {"symbol": "on", "gloss": "Resting atop.", "nl_synonyms": ["on top of"]}, {"symbol": "under", "gloss": "Beneath.", "nl_synonyms": ["below"]}, {"symbol": "next_to", "gloss": "Adjacent to.", "nl_synonyms": ["beside"]}, {"symbol": "left_of", "gloss": "To the left of.", "nl_synonyms": ["left of"]}, {"symbol": "right_of", "gloss": "To the right of.", "nl_synonyms": ["right of"]}, {"symbol": "in_front_of", "gloss": "Positioned in front of.", "nl_synonyms": ["in front of"]}, {"symbol": "behind", "gloss": "Positioned behind.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Put the bowl right of the spoon.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=\"bowl\") -> bowl : REF[STRING]\nACTION pick_up(target=\"spoon\") -> spoon : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=bowl, destination=spoon, relation=right_of)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the directional relations required by sampled household placement tasks.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "search-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical namespaced values for search, filtering, ranking, currency, genre, category, and availability attributes.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "rank_price", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: monetary cost.", "nl_synonyms": ["cheapest", "lowest price"]}, {"symbol": "rank_rating", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: user or critic score.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_distance", "gloss": "Rank field: proximity.", "nl_synonyms": ["nearest", "closest"]}, {"symbol": "dir_asc", "gloss": "Ascending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["lowest first"]}, {"symbol": "dir_desc", "gloss": "Descending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["highest first"]}, {"symbol": "curr_usd", "gloss": "United States dollar currency.", "nl_synonyms": ["$"]}, {"symbol": "cat_game", "gloss": "Category: video game.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cat_limited_time_offers", "gloss": "Category: time-limited deals.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "avail_in_stock", "gloss": "Available for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["available"]}, {"symbol": "avail_out_of_stock", "gloss": "Unavailable for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["sold out"]}], "membership_rule": "Members are prefixed by their facet: `rank_` for rank_field, `dir_` for rank_direction, `curr_` for currency, `genre_` for genre, `cat_` for category, `avail_` for availability. An attribute must only accept symbols with its corresponding prefix.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the cheapest mirror under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=\"mirror\", currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=rank_price, rank_direction=dir_asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds typed search and ranking vocabulary with globally unique namespaced symbols to ensure facet-specific lookups.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "role-recipient", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical social or organizational roles used as recipients and audiences.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "user", "gloss": "The requesting human.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "agent", "gloss": "The assistant.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "manager", "gloss": "The user's manager.", "nl_synonyms": ["boss"]}, {"symbol": "customer", "gloss": "A customer.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "professor", "gloss": "An instructor.", "nl_synonyms": ["teacher"]}, {"symbol": "support_agent", "gloss": "A customer-support representative.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A lowercase_underscore relationship or institutional role.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite email to my manager.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, content=\"follow-up\", tone=polite)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides an individually look-upable recipient category.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "tone-value", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of canonical tone values used by communication, utterance, and generation attributes.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "formal", "gloss": "Professional and conventional.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "polite", "gloss": "Courteous.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "neutral", "gloss": "Neither warm nor hostile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "urgent", "gloss": "Emphasizes time sensitivity.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "casual", "gloss": "Informal and relaxed.", "nl_synonyms": ["casually"]}, {"symbol": "friendly", "gloss": "Warm and approachable.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "empathetic", "gloss": "Shows understanding of feelings.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "firm", "gloss": "Clear and assertive.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apologetic", "gloss": "Expresses regret.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "persuasive", "gloss": "Intended to convince.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "humorous", "gloss": "Intended to amuse.", "nl_synonyms": ["funny"]}, {"symbol": "supportive", "gloss": "Offers encouragement or help.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Brief tone.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Detailed tone.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "When a symbol (e.g., detailed, concise) exists in multiple categories, it is resolved by the expected category of the attribute it binds to.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send a polite follow-up.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=manager, content=\"follow-up\", tone=polite)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the real glossary category already required by Action, Utterance, and Generate semantics, with a global disambiguation rule.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "artifact-specification", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical artifact targets and generation facets for format, style, locale, and duration units.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "story", "gloss": "Artifact: narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "short_text", "gloss": "Artifact: short constrained text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "technical_introduction", "gloss": "Artifact: introductory technical explanation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "contract", "gloss": "Artifact: agreement or contract.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_report", "gloss": "Artifact: headed report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "character_profile", "gloss": "Artifact: fictional character profile.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "scene", "gloss": "Artifact: dramatic or narrative scene.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "plan", "gloss": "Artifact: actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bullet_points", "gloss": "Format: bullet list.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "structured_sections", "gloss": "Format: headed sections.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "paragraph", "gloss": "Format: prose paragraph form.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "balanced", "gloss": "Style: presents competing perspectives fairly.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "detailed", "gloss": "Style: extensive detail.", "nl_synonyms": ["thorough"]}, {"symbol": "concise", "gloss": "Style: brief.", "nl_synonyms": ["brief"]}, {"symbol": "en_us", "gloss": "Locale: United States English.", "nl_synonyms": ["English"]}, {"symbol": "day", "gloss": "Duration unit: calendar day.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "hour", "gloss": "Duration unit: hour.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "week", "gloss": "Duration unit: seven-day week.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}], "membership_rule": "Each member belongs to exactly one facet: artifact target, format, style, locale, or duration unit. When a symbol (e.g., detailed) exists in multiple categories, it is resolved by the attribute's expected category.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write a balanced structured report for a two-week project.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=structured_report, content=\"project report\", duration=2, duration_unit=week, format=structured_sections, style=balanced) -> report : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds the missing artifact-type category and fixes duration by making its unit an explicit glossary value.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member\n\n-- Signatures and Result Categories (SAME, NEW, MEMBER, VALUE, NONE):\n-- open_page(target) -> NONE\n-- click(target) -> NONE\n-- select_filter(target, content) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- apply_filters(target, content) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- sort(target, rank_field, rank_direction) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- search_travel(origin, destination, date, [passengers, return_date]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- search_transit(origin, destination, [date, near]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- search_web(target, [audience_class, availability, category, color, currency, distance, genre, location, max_price, min_rating, shape, size]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- fill_field(target, content) -> NONE\n-- submit(target) -> NONE\n-- extract(target, limit) -> REF[T] or LIST[REF[T]] [MEMBER]\n-- read_page(target, [content]) -> STRING [VALUE]\n-- save_favorite(target) -> NONE\n-- add_to_cart(target) -> NONE\n-- pick_up(target, [source]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- place(target, destination, [destination_location, destination_relation, relation]) -> NONE\n-- heat(target, [destination]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- chill(target, [destination]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- rinse(target, destination) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- slice(target) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- pour(target, destination) -> NONE\n-- open_container(target) -> NONE\n-- close_container(target) -> NONE\n-- turn_on(target) -> NONE\n-- turn_off(target) -> NONE\n-- modify_code(target, [actual_output, argument, assertion, call, class, content, environment, expected_output, function, module, platform, reproduction_step]) -> NONE\n-- run_tests(target, [test_id]) -> NONE\n-- add_file(target, content) -> NONE\n-- delete_file(target) -> NONE\n-- send_email(recipient, content, [tone]) -> NONE\n-- send_message(recipient, content, [tone]) -> NONE\n-- call(recipient) -> NONE\n-- check_replied(target, deadline) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- file_age_days(target) -> NUMBER [VALUE]\n-- path_in_folder(target, destination) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- create_list(target) -> REF[STRING] [NEW]\n-- add_to_list(target, destination) -> NONE\n-- check_support_status(target, metric) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- offer_discount(target, [content, discount_percent]) -> NONE\n-- offer_expedited_shipping(target, [content]) -> NONE\n-- custom_<domain>_<verb>(target, [content, destination, instrument]) -> NONE", "semantics": "An Action attribute is valid only if it is an attribute-name member, its value conforms to the attribute's declared category/rule, and it is listed in that operation's signature. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (required first, then optional), with any optional attributes present sorted alphabetically by attribute name. When the source text does not impose a sequential order for independent steps, emit them in alphabetical order of their operations, breaking ties by target. Dedicated search attributes are canonical: a criterion represented by a dedicated attribute must not also appear in select_filter/apply_filters content. Handle naming rule: A bound REF IDENT must be the normalized singular head noun of the entity; a LIST[REF[T]] must be the plural. If a collision occurs, append a numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` in source order. Existing coreference behavior remains unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the lowest-priced mirror in stock under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=\"mirror\", availability=avail_in_stock, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=rank_price, rank_direction=dir_asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action now validates every attribute against the complete attribute index and an operation-specific signature, enforcing canonical attribute order and exhaustive signatures.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Enforces canonical attribute order, handle naming rules, and exhaustive operation signatures as required.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only target, audience, audience_role, content, duration, duration_unit, exclude, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (target first, followed by any optional attributes sorted alphabetically by attribute name). Independent sequential generated steps without a source-imposed order must be emitted in alphabetical order of their target values. target is required and must be an artifact-specification target member. Handle naming rule: The bound IDENT must reflect the target artifact's normalized noun (singular for STRING/NUMBER/BOOL, plural for LIST). If a collision occurs, append a numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` in source order. duration and duration_unit must occur together. content and exclude remain transitional STRING channels. All prior GENERATE result, REF prohibition, and exact quantity semantics remain unchanged.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Write ten funny short texts in English.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=short_text, content=\"about finding quahogs on a beach\", locale=en_us, quantity=10, tone=humorous) -> short_texts : LIST[STRING]"}, "glossary_gloss": "GENERATE now accepts only documented attributes, enforcing canonical attribute order and handle naming.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies normative Generate applicability, canonical ordering, handle naming, and exclude attribute.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary speech-act member\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value", "semantics": "Only audience, content, recipient, register_note, target, and tone are legal UTTER attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in alphabetical order by attribute name. Independent sequential UTTER steps without a source-imposed order must be emitted in alphabetical order of their speech acts. Handle naming rule: If bound via `->`, the IDENT must be `content` or `content_2`, `content_3` for collisions. tone and register_note remain mutually exclusive. content remains a transitional STRING payload during the vocabulary-building phase, and UTTER remains legal only inside a CONVO TURN.", "worked_example": {"nl": "User casually thanks the agent.", "braincode": "CONVO Thanks {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER acknowledge(content=\"Thanks\", recipient=agent, tone=casual)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance now uses the complete attribute gate and enforces canonical attribute ordering and handle naming.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Ensures the claimed attribute index is normatively complete for UTTER and enforces canonical ordering and handle naming.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N2"}]
Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The bundle makes substantial N2/N3/N7 progress by adding actual lexical categories and stricter operation signatures, but it is not logically ready to land. Its structural example is invalid, its open lexical rules depend on external English/WordNet judgments, and that dependency regresses hard note N5. The missing descriptive categories also leave several sampled closed constraints unrepresentable, so rework is required before acceptance.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "structural-word", "change": "Correct the worked example to a grammar-valid TASK: RETURN may only occur as the Task's final return_stmt, not inside an IF block. Also explicitly state that every retained lexical punctuation/form used by the full grammar is either a structural-word member or covered by a named lexical rule."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace WordNet and 'conceptually fitting' domain selection with a self-contained, glossary-defined deterministic mapping procedure. Define every `custom_` component as a category-defined atomic token rule, or defer custom operations while the vocabulary is being built; do not require an English dictionary or external lemmatizer."}, {"target": "entity-name", "change": "Do not define open entity membership by unspecified English head-noun extraction. Add the deferred independently look-upable entity-state, entity-modifier, position, platform-name, and location categories, with category-specific membership rules and synonym mappings; restrict entity-name to a self-contained atomic-symbol rule."}, {"target": "search-value", "change": "Make each open facet usable deterministically: either enumerate its currently supported members or define a semantic, self-contained membership/synonym rule for the suffix after `genre_`, `cat_`, and related prefixes. Add a platform category and legal search_web platform attribute so the Netflix constraint is representable."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Add the deferred descriptive categories needed by the simulations, including itinerary/day/stop/route/travel-time; transit stop-count, policy, and amenity; media venue/showtime/ticket/seat; typed compatibility and instrument relations; code file/method/property/call/assertion and expected-versus-actual behavior; revision/improvement; procedure/safety/escalation; academic/job-search goals; food/nutrition/meal structures; medical topic/audience constraints; and email/message/collaboration structures."}, {"target": "Action, Generate, and Utterance", "change": "Audit every worked example against the revised grammar and value rules, and state one single canonical rule for result handles that resolves SAME-result rebinding without relying on translator choice. Clarify whether quoted entity strings are a transitional exception or whether entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists."}]
Logic issues: ["The structural-word worked example is invalid: `RETURN one` occurs inside IF, but Task grammar permits RETURN only as the final `return_stmt` after steps.", "operation-vocabulary calls WordNet and asks translators to choose the first domain that 'conceptually fits'; neither operation selection nor lemmatization is self-contained or deterministic.", "entity-name's open membership rule requires English noun-phrase/head extraction and therefore does not define a self-contained lexical category.", "search-value says facets are prefix-separated but does not define how an unlisted suffix such as `comedy` becomes a valid genre member or how its natural-language synonyms map canonically.", "The Netflix/platform constraint and the table-in-the-corner location constraint cannot be represented by the legal revised Action signatures.", "The proposal leaves the prior promised facet split and broad descriptive-vocabulary expansion deferred, despite those categories being directly needed by the sampled simulations."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The added operation, entity, relation, artifact, recipient, and search facets improve coverage for simple household, search, and generation requests. However, key sampled constraints still have no usable category or operation field: Netflix/platform, pet/type filters, table-corner location, travel structures, code structure beyond opaque strings, and most domain-specific request structures. The revised Action signatures also remove the previous generic default-operation signature, so coverage now relies on an underspecified custom-operation mechanism."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Dedicated ranking, availability, currency, tone, duration-unit, and placement-relation fields preserve more structure in several closed tasks. Yet the proposed signatures leave platform and category-combination constraints unrepresentable, while many code, conversational, legal, and planning meanings remain undifferentiated STRING payloads; this is permitted in the current build phase but does not realize the intended descriptive-vocabulary expansion."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical attribute order, result signatures, namespaced search symbols, and handle suffix rules are useful progress. But `custom_<domain>_<verb>` depends on a translator's conceptual domain judgment and an external WordNet lemmatizer, while entity extraction depends on unspecified English head-noun analysis. Independent translations already disagree sharply on search target, genre spelling, binding names, whether heat returns a binding, and code-fix representation."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The glossary becomes substantially more useful through explicit structural tokens and several descriptive categories. It nevertheless remains incomplete for the retained grammar and claimed vocabulary categories: open entity, role, search, and artifact categories do not give a sufficiently precise self-contained membership procedure, and the invalid structural-word example cannot be parsed as a valid Task."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "For the household and search simulations, typed operations, relation values, typed ranking, and explicit result categories give a weaker executor better actionable structure than raw requests. The benefit is limited for software, planning, travel, and open conversational requests because their decisive content remains a broad STRING payload."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "operation-vocabulary, entity-name, spatial-relation, and Action signatures help. The explicit sequential source order retains the one-at-a-time constraint."}, {"item_id": "dev-embodied-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Rinse the mug in the sink, then put it in the coffee maker.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RinseThenPlace\nTASK RinseThenPlace {\n  ACTION rinse(target=mug, destination=sink) -> mug : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=mug, destination=coffee_maker, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "entity-name, spatial-relation, and the rinse/place signatures make the core task fully structured."}, {"item_id": "86afd67c-1bff-455c-baa7-e18dcb64b0f3", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Find comedy tv shows on netflix sorted by audience score.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindComedyShows\nTASK FindComedyShows {\n  ACTION search_web(target=\"tv_show\", genre=genre_comedy) -> tv_shows : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=tv_shows, rank_field=rank_rating, rank_direction=dir_desc) -> tv_shows_2 : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "search-value supplies ranking and, under N6, genre_comedy can be assumed in the genre facet. No signature attribute or separately look-upable platform category captures the Netflix constraint."}, {"item_id": "bf469f30-6628-4017-b963-672645d7feab", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Find the highest rated dog collar under 10 dollar.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindDogCollar\nTASK FindDogCollar {\n  ACTION search_web(target=\"dog_collar\", currency=curr_usd, max_price=10) -> dog_collars : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=dog_collars, rank_field=rank_rating, rank_direction=dir_desc) -> dog_collars_2 : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "max_price, currency, and rating sort are represented. The dog/pet-type restriction has no category or legal search_web attribute; encoding it in target conflates product kind and animal applicability."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_223758_523581#1", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Microwave a slice of apple and place it on the table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MicrowaveAppleSlice\nTASK MicrowaveAppleSlice {\n  ACTION slice(target=\"apple\") -> apple_slices : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=apple_slices, limit=1) -> apple_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=apple_slice, destination=microwave) -> apple_slice_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=apple_slice_2, destination=\"table\", relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "slice, extract, heat, and spatial-relation encode the requested goal. The generated handle suffix follows the proposed collision rule."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_224836_919680#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a microwaved slice of apple on the table in the corner.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceMicrowavedAppleSlice\nTASK PlaceMicrowavedAppleSlice {\n  ACTION slice(target=\"apple\") -> apple_slices : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=apple_slices, limit=1) -> apple_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=apple_slice, destination=microwave) -> apple_slice_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=apple_slice_2, destination=\"table\", relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The microwave and placement actions are expressible, but the qualifying location 'in the corner' is lost because there is no position/location category or legal structured location modifier."}, {"item_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-11578", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix LogisticRegressionCV probabilistic scoring so the LogisticRegression created in _log_reg_scoring_path inherits multi_class and uses multinomial probabilities rather than default OvR.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixLogisticScoring\nTASK FixLogisticScoring {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"sklearn/linear_model/logistic.py\", actual_output=\"scoring uses OvR probabilities because LogisticRegression defaults to multi_class=ovr\", argument=\"multi_class\", class=\"LogisticRegression\", content=\"pass multi_class when constructing LogisticRegression in _log_reg_scoring_path\", expected_output=\"scoring uses multinomial probabilities when multi_class is multinomial\", function=\"_log_reg_scoring_path\", module=\"sklearn.linear_model.logistic\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The retained STRING channels preserve the actionable software-fix request in this build phase. module/class/function/argument fields help, but expected/actual behavior remains opaque prose rather than a code-behavior vocabulary."}, {"item_id": "django__django-13112", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix makemigrations crashing for a ForeignKey when the Django app name has mixed case.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixMixedCaseForeignKey\nTASK FixMixedCaseForeignKey {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=\"django/db/models/fields/related.py\", actual_output=\"lazy ForeignKey reference uses dj_reglogin while installed app is DJ_RegLogin\", content=\"preserve mixed-case application-name resolution during migration and lazy reference handling\", expected_output=\"ForeignKey migration succeeds for an installed mixed-case app name\", platform=\"Django 3.1b1\", reproduction_step=\"run python3 manage.py migrate with DJ_RegLogin installed\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The current free STRING channels preserve the closed task's actionable core. Proposed code attributes organize some facets but do not structurally encode model, field, call, or assertion relationships."}, {"item_id": "c6516", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can you give me some great places to visit in the Netherlands?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT VisitNetherlands\nCONVO VisitNetherlands {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Recommend great places to visit in the Netherlands.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Utterance preserves the request speech act and recipient, but recommendation substance remains a transitional STRING payload; this is acceptable during the stated build phase."}, {"item_id": "c3388", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "yeah being in pain sucks, i have been in pain for nearly 3 years, can you tell me a joke to help take my mind off the pain", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PainDistraction\nCONVO PainDistraction {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"I have been in pain for nearly three years.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Tell me a joke to help take my mind off the pain.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation sequencing and speech acts are captured, but pain duration, requested joke content, and distraction relation remain prose. No medical-topic or support-response category is present."}, {"item_id": "c2067", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can you breifly explain American politics to me?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainAmericanPolitics\nCONVO ExplainAmericanPolitics {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Briefly explain American politics.\", recipient=agent, tone=concise)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request speech act, recipient, and brevity preference are captured, but the requested explanatory subject remains in content."}, {"item_id": "c2904", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Tell me about what is happening in New Zealand Politically", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT NewZealandPolitics\nCONVO NewZealandPolitics {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Explain current political developments in New Zealand.\", recipient=agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational request is structurally represented, but currentness, country, and political-topic semantics remain a prose payload."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-73283", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Introduce the topic of Impact of Dam Construction on Seasonal Precipitation Pattern, Land Use/Cover, and Socio-economic in the semi-arid Region, Eastern Sudan.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT IntroduceDamTopic\nTASK IntroduceDamTopic : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=technical_introduction, content=\"Impact of dam construction on seasonal precipitation patterns, land use/cover, and socio-economic conditions in semi-arid Eastern Sudan\") -> technical_introduction : STRING\n  RETURN technical_introduction\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "artifact-specification supplies a useful technical_introduction target, but the substantive topic stays in the permitted transitional STRING channel."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-76731", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "try to squeeze some ideas of The Holy Blood and the Holy Grail-alike conspiracy from The Brothers Karamazov", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CompareConspiracyThemes\nTASK CompareConspiracyThemes : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, content=\"Suggest conspiracy-like thematic parallels between The Brothers Karamazov and The Holy Blood and the Holy Grail\") -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The generation act is represented, while works, themes, comparison relation, and requested interpretive substance remain prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-137561", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Write about how they evolved.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainGloopiterEvolution\nTASK ExplainGloopiterEvolution : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=story, content=\"Write about the evolution of Gloopy, Glitter, and the inhabitants of Gloopiter.\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "artifact-specification supplies story, but the continuing fictional-world context and evolution subject are opaque content."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-78000", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Add a binding signature line.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReviseSpeakerContract\nTASK ReviseSpeakerContract : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=contract, content=\"Revise the speaker-to-client agreement by adding a binding client acceptance signature line and date line.\") -> contract : STRING\n  RETURN contract\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "contract is an added artifact target, but legal clauses, parties, signature semantics, and revision relation have no structured descriptive vocabulary."}, {"item_id": "1776009617894", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Can you suggest a posting schedule to help the channel grow quickly in its first month?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanChannelSchedule\nTASK PlanChannelSchedule : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=plan, content=\"Suggest a first-month posting schedule for the Hamoudi preschool educational YouTube channel to support growth.\") -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "plan is a useful artifact target, but channel, preschool audience, cadence, first-month duration, and growth goal are not represented by descriptive categories."}, {"item_id": "1775429344935", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Help me to create a text about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI. Only 100 words.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteJapanSGIText\nTASK WriteJapanSGIText : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=short_text, content=\"Write about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI\", quantity=100) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "short_text and exact quantity are structured by artifact-specification and Generate. The personal decision, Japan, SGI, and learning purpose remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775752130482", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "hello, i want to plan a 3 day safari in eastern cape south africa", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanEasternCapeSafari\nTASK PlanEasternCapeSafari : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=plan, content=\"Plan a safari in Eastern Cape, South Africa\", duration=3, duration_unit=day) -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "duration and duration_unit are now structured. Safari, itinerary, region, country, travel stops, lodging, and transport have no relevant descriptive categories."}, {"item_id": "1775479438859", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Gain a short certification if it opens a stable field examples in UK context?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SuggestUKCertifications\nTASK SuggestUKCertifications : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=structured_report, content=\"Give examples of short UK certifications that can lead to stable employment suitable for mortgage eligibility.\") -> structured_report : STRING\n  RETURN structured_report\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "structured_report is a useful artifact target, but UK jurisdiction, certifications, employment stability, mortgage criteria, and examples remain content prose."}]
