-- check_support_status(target, metric) -> BOOL [VALUE]
-- offer_discount(target, [content]) -> NONE
-- offer_expedited_shipping(target, [content]) -> NONE
-- custom_<domain>_<verb>(target, [content, destination]) -> NONE` — An Action attribute is valid only if it is an attribute-name member, its value conforms to the attribute's declared category/rule, and it is listed in that operation's signature. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (required first, then optional sorted alphabetically). Handle rule: When rebinding a SAME result or handling a collision, the canonical handle must be the original handle name with a sequentially incremented numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` appended, based strictly on source order, without relying on translator choice. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists.
- [revise] Generate: grammar `generation ::= "GENERATE" "(" generate-attr ("," generate-attr)* ")" "->" IDENT ":" gen_type
generate-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
gen_type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" gen_type"]"` — Only target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (target first, followed by optional attributes sorted alphabetically). Handle rule: The bound IDENT must reflect the target artifact's normalized noun. If a collision occurs, append a numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` in source order. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists. content remains a transitional STRING channel.
- [revise] Utterance: grammar `utterance ::= "UTTER" speech-act "(" utter-attr ("," utter-attr)* ")" ("->" IDENT)?
speech-act ::= operation-vocabulary member
utter-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value` — Only audience, content, recipient, target, and tone are legal UTTER attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in alphabetical order by attribute name. Handle rule: If bound via `->`, the IDENT must be `content` or `content_2`, `content_3` for collisions. Quoted strings are a transitional exception; symbols must be used when available. content remains a transitional STRING payload during the vocabulary-building phase, and UTTER remains legal only inside a CONVO TURN.

