he commute to work.\n*   **The 3 PM Coffee Compromise:** If you *love* an afternoon coffee, make it your **\"work shift starter\"**—a small one right when your shift begins. It gives you a lift without ruining sleep.\n*   **Hydration is Your Secret Sidekick:** Keep a water bottle with you *always*. Sometimes fatigue feels like hunger or a need for coffee, but it’s just dehydration.\n*   **Listen to Your Body:** On days you’re *exhausted* after work, **skip the evening study**. A 20-minute walk and early bed will make you more productive tomorrow than a forced 2-hour cram session.\n*   **Celebrate Your Rituals:** That morning coffee & cereal? That’s self-care. Enjoy it without guilt. It’s part of your success system.\n\n---\n\n### **Let's Fine-Tune This For YOU!**\n\nTo make the **afternoon coffee timing** and **evening wind-down** perfect, I just need:\n\n1.  **What time does your work shift actually start and end?** (e.g., 3 PM - 9 PM? 4 PM - 10 PM?)\n2.  **How long is your commute to work?** (Does the \"gap\" include travel time?)\n3.  **What time do you *ideally* want to be asleep on school nights?**\n\n**Example:** If work is 4 PM-10 PM with a 15-min commute, your last coffee should be **by 3:30 PM** to be safe for an 11 PM bedtime. We can adjust!\n\n**You’re not just building a schedule—you’re designing a sustainable, enjoyable rhythm.** Now, let’s plug in your exact times and make this plan fit you like your favorite cozy sweater. 😊\n\n**What are your exact work hours and commute?**",
