collaboration_structure", "gloss": "Collaboration structure.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Maps attributes to their permitted value categories. `platform` uses `platform-name`. `location`, `destination` use `location-name` or `entity-name`. `relation` uses `spatial-relation`. Search facets use `search-value`. Descriptive domain attributes (roles, tones, artifacts, modifiers, states, travel, code, medical) use `descriptive-value`. `target` uses `entity-name`. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Search comedy tv shows on netflix.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=tv_show, genre=genre_comedy, platform=netflix) -> tv_shows : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Audited index of attributes, including the requested domain attributes, explicitly mapping each to its permitted value category.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "entity-name", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical entity base nouns.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mug", "gloss": "Drinking cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rag", "gloss": "Cleaning cloth.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tub", "gloss": "Bathtub.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "book", "gloss": "Reading material.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mirror", "gloss": "Reflective item.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sink", "gloss": "Washing basin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "counter", "gloss": "Countertop surface.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cupboard", "gloss": "Storage cabinet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "refrigerator", "gloss": "Cooling appliance.", "nl_synonyms": ["fridge"]}, {"symbol": "spoon", "gloss": "Eating utensil.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "bowl", "gloss": "A bowl.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "pillow", "gloss": "A cushion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sofa", "gloss": "A couch.", "nl_synonyms": ["couch"]}, {"symbol": "armchair", "gloss": "A chair with armrests.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet_paper", "gloss": "Toilet paper.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "holder", "gloss": "A holder.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "wall", "gloss": "A wall.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "motherboard", "gloss": "Computer motherboard.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "processor", "gloss": "Computer processor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "decorative_led_candles", "gloss": "LED candles.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cup", "gloss": "A cup.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "coffee_maker", "gloss": "Coffee machine.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "microwave", "gloss": "Microwave oven.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "toilet", "gloss": "A toilet.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "apple", "gloss": "An apple.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tv_show", "gloss": "Television program.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dog_collar", "gloss": "Collar for a dog.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A self-contained atomic-symbol rule: an entity-name is an exact symbol matching `[a-z_]+` representing a discrete entity class. It does not rely on unspecified English head-noun extraction. If a member exists, it must be used instead of a quoted string.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Pick up the rag.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=rag) -> rag : REF[STRING]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Provides base entity nouns with a self-contained atomic symbol rule, removing the English-extraction dependency.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "search-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical namespaced values for search, filtering, ranking, currency, genre, category, and availability attributes.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "rank_price", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: monetary cost.", "nl_synonyms": ["cheapest", "lowest price"]}, {"symbol": "rank_rating", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: user or critic score.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_distance", "gloss": "Rank field: proximity.", "nl_synonyms": ["nearest", "closest"]}, {"symbol": "dir_asc", "gloss": "Ascending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["lowest first"]}, {"symbol": "dir_desc", "gloss": "Descending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["highest first"]}, {"symbol": "curr_usd", "gloss": "United States dollar currency.", "nl_synonyms": ["$"]}, {"symbol": "cat_game", "gloss": "Category: video game.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cat_limited_time_offers", "gloss": "Category: time-limited deals.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "avail_in_stock", "gloss": "Available for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["available"]}, {"symbol": "avail_out_of_stock", "gloss": "Unavailable for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["sold out"]}, {"symbol": "genre_comedy", "gloss": "Genre: comedy.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Each open facet is usable deterministically: members are prefixed by `rank_`, `dir_`, `curr_`, `genre_`, `cat_`, `avail_`. The suffix must be a self-contained atomic `[a-z_]+` string (e.g., `genre_comedy`). Translators map to known symbols or emit the atomic rule directly.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the cheapest mirror under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=rank_price, rank_direction=dir_asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Adds typed search and ranking vocabulary with a deterministic, self-contained suffix rule.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "spatial-relation", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of relations used when placing one entity relative to another.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "in", "gloss": "Contained within.", "nl_synonyms": ["inside"]}, {"symbol": "on", "gloss": "Resting atop.", "nl_synonyms": ["on top of"]}, {"symbol": "under", "gloss": "Beneath.", "nl_synonyms": ["below"]}, {"symbol": "next_to", "gloss": "Adjacent to.", "nl_synonyms": ["beside"]}, {"symbol": "left_of", "gloss": "To the left of.", "nl_synonyms": ["left of"]}, {"symbol": "right_of", "gloss": "To the right of.", "nl_synonyms": ["right of"]}, {"symbol": "in_front_of", "gloss": "Positioned in front of.", "nl_synonyms": ["in front of"]}, {"symbol": "behind", "gloss": "Positioned behind.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Put the bowl right of the spoon.", "braincode": "ACTION pick_up(target=bowl) -> bowl : REF[STRING]\nACTION pick_up(target=spoon) -> spoon : REF[STRING]\nACTION place(target=bowl, destination=spoon, relation=right_of)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Supplies the directional relations required by sampled household placement tasks.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "platform-name", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical platform, brand, and software environment names.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "netflix", "gloss": "Streaming platform.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "django", "gloss": "Web framework.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "sklearn", "gloss": "Machine learning library.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "youtube", "gloss": "Video platform.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `[a-z_]+` representing a software platform, service, or brand.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find comedy tv shows on netflix.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=tv_show, genre=genre_comedy, platform=netflix) -> tv_shows : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides the requested independent platform category for constraints like Netflix.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "location-name", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical physical and conceptual locations, positions, and areas.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "corner", "gloss": "A corner area.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "table", "gloss": "A table surface.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "eastern_cape", "gloss": "Eastern Cape region.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "japan", "gloss": "Country of Japan.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `[a-z_]+` representing a physical or conceptual location, position, or area.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Place it on the table in the corner.", "braincode": "ACTION place(target=apple_slice, destination=table, location=corner, relation=on)"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Provides the requested independent location category for constraints like the table corner.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "descriptive-value", "glossary_gloss": "A unified category for roles, tones, artifacts, modifiers, states, and domain concepts.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "role_user", "gloss": "The requesting human.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "role_agent", "gloss": "The assistant.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "role_manager", "gloss": "The user's manager.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone_polite", "gloss": "Courteous.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone_casual", "gloss": "Informal.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone_concise", "gloss": "Brief.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_story", "gloss": "Narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_short_text", "gloss": "Short text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_plan", "gloss": "Actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_structured_report", "gloss": "Headed report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mod_mixed_case", "gloss": "Mixed case modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state_microwaved", "gloss": "Microwaved state.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_safari", "gloss": "Safari concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_pain", "gloss": "Pain concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_ovr", "gloss": "One-vs-rest concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_sgi", "gloss": "SGI concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_day", "gloss": "Day unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A unified category for roles, tones, artifacts, modifiers, states, and domain concepts. Members are prefixed: `role_`, `tone_`, `art_`, `mod_`, `state_`, `dom_`. The suffix is an atomic `[a-z_]+` string. Added to satisfy the need for descriptive categories within the 12-change limit.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3 day safari.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", duration=3, duration_unit=dom_day) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Consolidates the requested descriptive domains, states, and modifiers into a single category to fit the 12-change limit.", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Action", "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member\n\n-- Signatures and Result Categories (SAME, NEW, MEMBER, VALUE, NONE):\n-- open_page(target) -> NONE\n-- click(target) -> NONE\n-- select_filter(target, content) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- apply_filters(target, content) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- sort(target, rank_field, rank_direction) -> LIST[REF[T]] [SAME]\n-- search_travel(origin, destination, date, [passengers, return_date]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- search_transit(origin, destination, [date, location]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- search_web(target, [availability, category, currency, genre, location, max_price, min_rating, platform]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- fill_field(target, content) -> NONE\n-- submit(target) -> NONE\n-- extract(target, limit) -> REF[T] or LIST[REF[T]] [MEMBER]\n-- read_page(target, [content]) -> STRING [VALUE]\n-- save_favorite(target) -> NONE\n-- add_to_cart(target) -> NONE\n-- pick_up(target, [source]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- place(target, destination, [location, relation]) -> NONE\n-- heat(target, [destination]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- chill(target, [destination]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- rinse(target, destination) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- slice(target) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- pour(target, destination) -> NONE\n-- open_container(target) -> NONE\n-- close_container(target) -> NONE\n-- turn_on(target) -> NONE\n-- turn_off(target) -> NONE\n-- modify_code(target, [actual_output, assertion, call, content, expected_output, file, method, property, reproduction_step]) -> NONE\n-- run_tests(target, [file]) -> NONE\n-- add_file(target, content) -> NONE\n-- delete_file(target) -> NONE\n-- send_email(recipient, content, [tone]) -> NONE\n-- send_message(recipient, content, [tone]) -> NONE\n-- call(recipient) -> NONE\n-- check_replied(target, deadline) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- file_age_days(target) -> NUMBER [VALUE]\n-- path_in_folder(target, destination) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- create_list(target) -> REF[STRING] [NEW]\n-- add_to_list(target, destination) -> NONE\n-- check_support_status(target, metric) -> BOOL [VALUE]\n-- offer_discount(target, [content]) -> NONE\n-- offer_expedited_shipping(target, [content]) -> NONE\n-- custom_<domain>_<verb>(target, [content, destination]) -> NONE", "semantics": "An Action attribute is valid only if it is an attribute-name member, its value conforms to the attribute's declared category/rule, and it is listed in that operation's signature. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (required first, then optional sorted alphabetically). Handle rule: When rebinding a SAME result or handling a collision, the canonical handle must be the original handle name with a sequentially incremented numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` appended, based strictly on source order, without relying on translator choice. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Microwave a slice of apple and place it on the table in the corner.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceMicrowavedAppleSlice\nTASK PlaceMicrowavedAppleSlice {\n  ACTION slice(target=apple) -> apple_slices : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=apple_slices, limit=1) -> apple_slice : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=apple_slice, destination=microwave) -> apple_slice_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=apple_slice_2, destination=table, location=corner, relation=on)\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Action now validates every attribute against the complete attribute index and an operation-specific signature, enforcing canonical attribute order, exhaustive signatures, and a deterministic handle suffix rule.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Enforces canonical attribute order, handle suffix rules, and explicit platform/location attributes as required.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (target first, followed by optional attributes sorted alphabetically). Handle rule: The bound IDENT must reflect the target artifact's normalized noun. If a collision occurs, append a numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` in source order. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists. content remains a transitional STRING channel.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Help me to create a text about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI. Only 100 words.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteJapanSGIText\nTASK WriteJapanSGIText : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"Write about my decision to go to Japan to learn about SGI\", quantity=100) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "GENERATE now accepts only documented attributes, enforcing canonical attribute order and a deterministic handle suffix rule.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Supplies normative Generate applicability, canonical ordering, and handle naming.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N2"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Utterance", "grammar": "utterance ::= \"UTTER\" speech-act \"(\" utter-attr (\",\" utter-attr)* \")\" (\"->\" IDENT)?\nspeech-act ::= operation-vocabulary member\nutter-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value", "semantics": "Only audience, content, recipient, target, and tone are legal UTTER attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in alphabetical order by attribute name. Handle rule: If bound via `->`, the IDENT must be `content` or `content_2`, `content_3` for collisions. Quoted strings are a transitional exception; symbols must be used when available. content remains a transitional STRING payload during the vocabulary-building phase, and UTTER remains legal only inside a CONVO TURN.", "worked_example": {"nl": "I have been in pain for nearly 3 years.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PainDistraction\nCONVO PainDistraction {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"I have been in pain for nearly three years.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Utterance now uses the complete attribute gate and enforces canonical attribute ordering and handle naming.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Ensures the claimed attribute index is normatively complete for UTTER and enforces canonical ordering and handle naming.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N2"}], "_provider_used": "gemini", "_model_used": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The new operation, entity, search, platform, location, and spatial-relation inventories cover several previously unsupported household, shopping, and code concepts. However, revised Action removes the previous default-operation fallback and does not supply signatures for many existing or newly listed concepts, while the generic file-list input task remains inexpressible; this creates coverage regressions or failures."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The additions preserve more distinctions for search ranking, spatial placement, code reports, and generated-artifact requests. But descriptive-value is an over-broad union: tone, role, artifact, state, domain concept, and modifier values are interchangeable under the stated attribute mapping, so it cannot preserve the intended type of a constraint such as a tone versus an artifact or entity state."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical attribute ordering and numeric rebinding suffixes improve convergence where a valid operation signature exists. Determinism remains poor for arbitrary custom_<domain>_<action>, entity-name, platform-name, location-name, descriptive-value, and facet suffixes: their rules specify token shape but no canonical NL-to-token mapping, segmentation rule, synonym table, or criterion for choosing a domain/category."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "A categorized glossary is a substantial improvement over construct-only entries, and spatial/search members are readable. The unified descriptive-value category harms lookupability because a reader cannot infer which conceptual value set a given attribute permits, and several attribute mappings group unrelated semantic types into one category."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "Typed operation signatures, relation values, filter/rank values, and explicit code-report attributes would give a weaker agent useful planning structure for supported requests. The benefit is limited by invalid examples, missing signatures, and residual opaque content strings."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-code-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Given a list of file paths, delete every file older than 30 days unless it's in the 'archive' folder.", "braincode": "GAP[entrypoint TASK cannot accept the requested file_paths input; no input-binding construct exists]", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "Action vocabulary retains file_age_days, path_in_folder, and delete_file, but the entrypoint rule still requires a zero-parameter TASK."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftExtension\nTASK DraftExtension : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"Reply asking professor for a two-day extension on assignment\", duration=2, duration_unit=dom_day, tone=tone_formal) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Generate has no defined tone_formal member, and the substantive request remains prose in content; descriptive-value only provides tone_polite, tone_casual, and tone_concise."}, {"item_id": "b7082615-e6e1-4981-b51b-9259671d1adf", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Change your store to the one nearest to 07055", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ChangeStore\nTASK ChangeStore {\n  ACTION search_web(target=store, location=\"07055\") -> stores : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION sort(target=stores, rank_field=rank_distance, rank_direction=dir_asc) -> stores_2 : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION extract(target=stores_2, limit=1) -> store : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION click(target=store)\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "search_web and ranking are now representable, but no operation means set the selected store, and ZIP code is still an untyped quoted payload."}, {"item_id": "e2adf8f1-547d-4671-96c1-4a21a56e135d", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "View the upcoming schedule from Otis St@Summer St to City Point of the transit near South Station for today.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ViewTransitSchedule\nTASK ViewTransitSchedule CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION search_transit(origin=\"Otis St@Summer St\", destination=\"City Point\", location=\"South Station\", date=\"2025-06-03\") -> schedules : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  ACTION read_page(target=schedules, content=\"upcoming schedule\") -> schedule : STRING\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "search_transit captures origin, destination, location, and date, but the schedule criterion remains prose and South Station is not a location-name symbol."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_120422_949453#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Move a red rag into a sink.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MoveRedRag\nTASK MoveRedRag {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=rag) -> rag : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=rag, destination=sink, relation=in)\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "spatial-relation enables in, but red is lost: modifier accepts the undifferentiated descriptive-value category and no red/mod_red member is supplied."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190906_165121_524545#3", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a box with keys in it on a chair.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceBox\nTASK PlaceBox {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=keys) -> keys : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=keys, destination=box, relation=in)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=box) -> box : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=box, destination=chair, relation=on)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The proposed open entity-name rule can hold box, keys, and chair, while spatial-relation captures both containment and placement."}, {"item_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-7757", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "The default value for positional only argument has vanished.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixPositionalDefault\nTASK FixPositionalDefault {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=sphinx, file=\"sphinx/util/inspect.py\", reproduction_step=\"py:function foo(a, b=0, /, c=1)\", expected_output=\"default value 0 shown for b\", actual_output=\"default value vanished\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=sphinx)\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "New code attributes improve structure, but file path, call syntax, assertion, and expected/actual behavior remain free prose strings rather than typed symbolic structures."}, {"item_id": "django__django-15268", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Optimize multiple AlterFooTogether operations into one.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT OptimizeAlterTogether\nTASK OptimizeAlterTogether {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=\"django/db/migrations/operations/models.py\", content=\"coalesce consecutive AlterUniqueTogether and AlterIndexTogether remove/add operations into one final operation\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django)\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "modify_code is available, but no symbolic code-operation, class, function, transformation, or equivalence structure encodes the requested optimization."}, {"item_id": "c7033", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "What is an objectively stronger video game, Marvel's Spider-Man 2 or Baldur's Gate 3?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CompareGames\nCONVO CompareGames {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Choose the objectively stronger video game: Marvel's Spider-Man 2 or Baldur's Gate 3\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation structure and speech act are preserved, but comparison criteria and named games remain prose payload."}, {"item_id": "c1182", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "how to approach a girl", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DatingAdvice\nCONVO DatingAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"How to approach a girl\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "UTTER ask captures the request form but not its advice topic, constraints, or later revision context."}, {"item_id": "c224", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Why does it seem a lot of