es": "art_script and a 17+ rating value are absent; target and content therefore rely on open invented/prose values."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-113201", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Rewrite this table of profitable online earning methods to be comprehensive, preserve the first column, remove br tags, and output a table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RewriteMethodsTable\nTASK RewriteMethodsTable : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_structured_report, content=\"Rewrite supplied online-earning-method table; preserve first column; replace br tags with line breaks; make comprehensive and detailed; output a table\") -> structured_report : STRING\n  RETURN structured_report\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "art_structured_report helps only at a coarse level; table schema, preservation constraint, transformation operation, and source table are prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-155336", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Give me a summarize.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT SummarizeMonetag\nTASK SummarizeMonetag : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"Summarize the preceding Monetag review\") -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested speech act is only implicit in prose; no summarize operation, source-reference relation, or summary artifact category is defined."}, {"item_id": "1776020181361", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "My laptop (mac book pro 2017) gets hot and the fan starts to make noise when I am working. What can I do to reduce that", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT LaptopAdvice\nCONVO LaptopAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Advise how to reduce heat and fan noise on a 2017 MacBook Pro while working\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The advice request is captured as an ask, but device, symptoms, constraints, diagnosis, and recommendations remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775963744772", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Okay I see, so it's not really realistic for me to learn all that in a month. I do specifically want to learn jazz and classical music though, so please focus your advice on that.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PianoAdviceRevision\nCONVO PianoAdviceRevision {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Recommend beginner piano steps\")\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REVISES t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Focus advice on learning classical and jazz piano; one-month mastery is not expected\")\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "REVISES preserves the correction sequence, but music genres, beginner status, timeframe, and learning-plan constraints remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775837106479", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Thank you. Please help me come up with the invite what should I write.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT BirthdayInvite\nTASK BirthdayInvite : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, content=\"Write a birthday invitation for a nine-year-old's princess-themed party this week at a play venue for 10 adults and 20 children\") -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The generation request is represented, but event type, audience, party facts, schedule, venue, and invitation format are not symbolically structured."}, {"item_id": "1775973360170", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "planning my weekly daysas l go to school and work", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WeeklyPlan\nTASK WeeklyPlan : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Create a friendly weekly plan for school from morning to 2 PM and work from 4 PM to 8 PM, incorporating cereal and strong coffee in the morning and a late-morning snack\") -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "art_plan identifies the requested artifact, but temporal schedule, meals, work/school commitments, friendliness, and resource constraints remain prose."}], "cross_check": {"used": true, "agreement": "low", "notes": "Independent translations diverge materially. For the store task Anthropic reports a gap while Gemini uses search/sort/extract/click; for the red-rag task one omits red and one identifies a missing modifier; for open requests Anthropic reports vocabulary gaps while Gemini emits prose payloads. The proposal's broad open-token rules do not resolve these choices."}, "required_changes": [{"target": "attribute-name and descriptive-value", "change": "Replace the unified descriptive-value union with independently look-upable, attribute-specific categories at minimum for role/recipient, tone/register, artifact format/type, entity modifier, entity state, travel/transit, media/venue, code structure/behavior, medical topic/audience, planning/education, and message/collaboration structure. For every attribute, state its exact permitted category or literal rule; do not let tone accept artifact/state/domain values."}, {"target": "operation-vocabulary", "change": "Replace custom_<domain>_<action>'s token-shape-only rule with a deterministic mapping algorithm that specifies canonical domain selection, canonical action decomposition, component boundaries, and synonym mapping; alternatively defer custom operations. A regex alone does not define how a translator maps an NL operation to a canonical token."}, {"target": "entity-name, platform-name, location-name, search-value", "change": "Give each open category a category-specific canonical membership and synonym procedure, not merely '[a-z_]+' plus an English semantic description. Define how proper names, postal codes, paths, and multiword names are represented, and define canonical tokens for supported values such as red, formal, script, table, and ZIP/postal-code locations."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Restore coverage for all operations expressible under the current Action default signature, or enumerate valid signatures for every operation-vocabulary member. Add a defined operation for selecting/setting a store and define signatures for any listed operation usable as ACTION. Do not silently make formerly expressible default operations invalid."}, {"target": "Action, Generate, and Utterance", "change": "Audit and correct all examples and cross-references against revised grammar/value rules. In particular, define tone_formal before using it, define art_script before using it, state a complete value grammar, and make the entity-string transitional exception consistent with each operation's typed signature."}, {"target": "structural-word", "change": "Make the lexical inventory actually exhaustive for the retained grammar: reconcile ISO_DATE's quoted-string grammar with its lexical definition, include or define UNSIGNED_INT/HEX and every referenced lexical nonterminal, and give reserved-word collision treatment for category members and IDENT."}, {"target": "basis", "change": "Add a typed external-input/parameter mechanism for entrypoint tasks, or a defined document-input binding, so requests over a supplied list such as file paths can be expressed by a valid executable entrypoint."}], "logic_issues": ["descriptive-value makes semantically incompatible values legal for the same mapped attributes: tone can receive art_story, role_manager, state_microwaved, or dom_safari under the stated rules.", "The custom operation, entity, platform, location, descriptive, and search suffix rules define only syntax, not deterministic natural-language membership or canonicalization; arbitrary translators can emit distinct valid symbols for the same meaning.", "Revised Action's closed operation-id production and limited signature table remove the previous default signature for unlisted operations, regressing existing coverage without a migration rule.", "operation-vocabulary includes speech acts such as ask and inform but Action has no signatures for them, while Utterance accepts any operation-vocabulary member rather than a separately constrained speech-act category.", "The Action worked example uses entity values and list/result handles whose category/value typing is not fully defined by the proposal; its claimed exhaustive validation therefore cannot be mechanically applied.", "Generate's worked example uses tone/formal-like semantics elsewhere, while the supplied descriptive-value inventory lacks tone_formal; the PATHs script requires art_script, also absent.", "The structural-word proposal calls ISO_DATE a bare lexical form although the retained Task grammar defines it as a matching STRING literal, leaving two incompatible readings.", "The store task can locate and click a store but has no operation that changes the current store selection, so the requested final state is not encoded."], "notes_assessment": {"N2": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "The glossary moves substantially toward a complete lexicon by adding structural, action, entity, attribute, relation, search, platform, location, and descriptive categories. It remains incomplete and insufficiently categorized: several retained lexical forms are unresolved, attribute value categories are conflated, and required descriptive domains are not independently look-upable."}, "N3": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Many attributes now point to a named category, which is progress. The mapping is not complete or type-safe: broad groups permit incompatible values, some needed values are absent, and quoted transitional strings remain without attribute-specific literal rules."}, "N7": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Canonical attribute ordering and numeric handle suffixes are real improvements. Open category regexes and custom operation construction lack a canonical NL mapping and synonym policy, so one meaning can still yield many distinct expressions."}, "N1": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "The proposal supplies glossary categories and lexical rules for more tokens, but STRING and open identifiers remain by design in this build phase. This is not a regression because N2 explicitly preserves those channels until the closing phase."}, "N4": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "Prose content remains in Action, GENERATE, and UTTER STRING channels as required during N2's build phase; the proposal does not add further prose channels beyond those already retained."}, "N5": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Replacing WordNet/head-noun extraction with token-shape rules is progress toward self-containment. The semantic instructions 'representing' an entity, platform, location, or domain still leave English-dependent classification and canonicalization undefined."}, "N6": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "The grammar begins to refer to vocabulary categories rather than individual words. It still reshapes behavior around missing members and falls back to prose strings for many missing category/value distinctions instead of defining the categories needed by the simulations."}, "N8": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Search facets, placement relations, code attributes, and artifact values add useful distinctions. The merged descriptive category collapses distinctions at the type level, and missing categories lose important task constraints."}}, "rebuttal_rulings": [{"target": "attribute-name", "ruling": "overruled", "reasoning": "The twelve-change budget does not justify replacing independently look-upable semantic categories with one category that permits invalid cross-category values. The stated N2 requirement expressly requires descriptive vocabulary categories and look-upable entries; category-specific membership rules are necessary for N3 and N7 as well."}, {"target": "entity-descriptor and facet vocabularies", "ruling": "overruled", "reasoning": "platform-name and location-name are useful partial compliance, but states/modifiers and positions folded into descriptive-value are not independently constrained or look-upable by their attributes. The entity-name regex also does not establish canonical semantic membership or synonym mapping."}], "accept_changes": ["spatial-relation"], "chosen_position": null, "position_comparison": null, "reasoning": "[Forced acceptance after 3 attempt(s) without a clean accept — the required changes below are known issues carried forward for a future sprint to address, not resolved.] This is meaningful progress on the N2 glossary objective, especially through structural vocabulary and spatial/search categories, and it does not regress the build-phase permission for STRING channels. It cannot be accepted because the central unified descriptive category is type-unsound, the open-token rules do not determine canonical encoding, and revised Action removes previously available fallback coverage. The self-contained spatial-relation vocabulary is sound and may land independently."}
