**Membership rule:** A self-contained atomic-symbol rule: an entity-name is an exact symbol matching `[a-z_]+` representing a discrete entity class. It does not rely on unspecified English head-noun extraction. If a member exists, it must be used instead of a quoted string.

**Example:**
- NL: "Pick up the rag."
