   "model (command-light, score=64): It sounds like your grandmother displays problematic communication patterns. It is understandable that you would feel affected by such interactions and would seek support in these moments. \n\nIs there a specific aspect of these situations that you would like feedback on or would like assistance in understanding and addressing? Perhaps there could be dialogue or communication prompts you would like to implement in the future to improve the environment between you and your grandmother or to have better support on her part. \n\nIt is crucial that in such situations you have support in your corner, whether that be from friends, family, or mental health professionals who can guide you through navigating these relationships. \n\nIs there another angle you would like my assistance with or would like to discuss further?",
   "model (command-light, score=49): I understand how difficult it is to face a difficult grandmother who does not treat you kindly. It is understandable that you would seek a different dynamic with her.\n\nThis situation requires addressing directly to your grandmother. It may be worthwhile to have a conversation with her in which you express your feelings and needs openly. During the discussion, it is crucial to express yourself clearly and confidently, and settle for no blame or guilt tactics. It might also help to openly document the problems you have observed, and frame the conversation as an opportunity for change, with a joint effort to improve the relationship. \n\nIt is imperative that you shall only engage with such dialogue when you feel comfortable and stable enough in order to handle any potential responses or confrontations. It is also worth seeking support of the rest of the family in this, by suggesting to have regular check-ins for the family where topics regarding the elderly generation can be brought and discussed safely and supported by professionals or close friends. \n\nIs there any aspect of this situation or your feelings surrounding it that you would like feedback on or would like me to comment upon?",
   "user (None, score=None): The rest of my family usually just ignores it and let's her act as she wants... There's not much help in that",
