   "model (command-light, score=68): It can be incredibly difficult and disheartening when those around you are unwilling or unable to address a problematic person or situation. It can seem like there's not much support in those situations but it is important to remember that you have chosen to prioritize your well-being and deal with these situations in a healthy way. \n\nIt is imperative that in moments where you feel unsupported or affected by others, you take safeguards and seek assistance yourself. This can include reaching out to friends, seeking support from professional counselors or mental health resources, or using strategies and techniques from counseling or support services to provide yourself with healthy ways of handling these situations. \n\nIt is amazing that you recognize the need to protect your well-being in this scenario and seek support from others. Is there any specific resource or activity you engage in that gives you a sense of support or comfort when feeling affected by the situation with your grandmother?",
