ent/audience previously used quoted strings (e.g. recipient=\"manager\") with no glossary value set; role_manager etc. already existed scattered in descriptive-value but not indexed as the recipient attribute's own category, violating N3's per-attribute entry requirement.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "search-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical namespaced values for ranking, sort-direction, genre, category, and availability attributes (currency now lives in its own currency-value category).", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "rank_price", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: monetary cost.", "nl_synonyms": ["cheapest", "lowest price"]}, {"symbol": "rank_rating", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: user or critic score.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_distance", "gloss": "Rank field: proximity.", "nl_synonyms": ["nearest", "closest"]}, {"symbol": "dir_asc", "gloss": "Ascending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["lowest first"]}, {"symbol": "dir_desc", "gloss": "Descending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["highest first"]}, {"symbol": "cat_game", "gloss": "Category: video game.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cat_limited_time_offers", "gloss": "Category: time-limited deals.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "avail_in_stock", "gloss": "Available for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["available"]}, {"symbol": "avail_out_of_stock", "gloss": "Unavailable for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["sold out"]}, {"symbol": "genre_comedy", "gloss": "Genre: comedy.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Each open facet is usable deterministically: members are prefixed by `rank_`, `dir_`, `genre_`, `cat_`, `avail_`. The suffix must be a self-contained atomic `[a-z_]+` string. Currency values no longer belong here; use currency-value.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the highest-rated in-stock comedy game.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=game, genre=genre_comedy, category=cat_game, availability=avail_in_stock) -> games : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=games, rank_field=rank_rating, rank_direction=dir_desc) -> sorted_games : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Splitting currency out into its own attribute-scoped category (currency-value) keeps each attribute's value set separately look-upable per N3, rather than bundled into one mixed-prefix facet bucket.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "descriptive-value", "glossary_gloss": "Artifact-type, modifier, and domain-concept symbols not covered by a dedicated attribute-value category (roles and tones now have their own categories).", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "art_story", "gloss": "Narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_short_text", "gloss": "Short text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_plan", "gloss": "Actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_structured_report", "gloss": "Headed report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "mod_mixed_case", "gloss": "Mixed case modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state_microwaved", "gloss": "Microwaved state.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_safari", "gloss": "Safari concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_pain", "gloss": "Pain concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_ovr", "gloss": "One-vs-rest concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_sgi", "gloss": "SGI concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A residual category for artifact-type (`art_`), entity-modifier (`mod_`), entity-state (`state_`), and domain-concept (`dom_`) symbols not yet promoted to their own attribute-value category. Units now live in duration-unit-value, roles in recipient-value, tones in tone-value — this category must not be used for those.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a safari.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Pulling role_ and tone_ and dom_day out into their dedicated attribute categories leaves descriptive-value as a narrower, still-open bucket for artifact/modifier/state/domain concepts, consistent with N3's requirement that every attribute have its own traceable value set instead of one catch-all.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes, validated against their attribute-name rules: target and audience use descriptive-value/recipient-value symbols respectively as applicable, duration_unit uses duration-unit-value, format uses format-value, tone uses tone-value; duration and quantity are NUMBER. Canonical ordering rule: Attributes must be emitted in exactly their declared signature order (target first, followed by optional attributes sorted alphabetically). Handle rule: The bound IDENT must reflect the target artifact's normalized noun. If a collision occurs, append a numeric suffix `_2`, `_3` in source order. Quoted entity strings are a transitional exception; entity-name symbols must be used whenever a member exists. content remains a transitional STRING channel pending N4's closing phase.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3 day safari.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanSafari\nTASK PlanSafari : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day) -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}"}, "change_type": "PATCH", "rationale": "Updates GENERATE's worked example and duration_unit cross-reference to the new duration-unit-value category instead of the retired dom_day symbol, keeping the construct consistent with the split vocabulary.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Flow-If", "grammar": "flow_if ::= \"IF\" check \"THEN\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" ( \"ELSE\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" )?", "semantics": "Conditional branching, used identically inside TASK and CONVO TURN bodies (both use the same `step` production). The Check is evaluated first, at the moment control reaches the IF. If true, the THEN block's steps execute in order; if false and an ELSE block is present, its steps execute instead; if false with no ELSE, control passes to whatever step follows. Flow-If may nest inside another Flow-If's THEN/ELSE or inside a FOR-EACH body; nested Checks evaluate only when outer control flow actually reaches them, never speculatively. THEN and ELSE each open their own fresh child variable scope under Task's unified scoping model: each may read any name already visible from the enclosing scope, but a LET/`->` binding made inside THEN is not visible inside ELSE, after the IF, or from any sibling construct, and vice versa. Because `step` now includes `utterance`, an IF nested inside a TURN body may contain UTTER in its branches exactly as it may contain ACTION; the same nesting containing UTTER inside a TASK body remains a static error per Utterance's restriction. When a Flow-If's Check depends on a preceding `check_replied` result with a future `deadline` instant, the branch's evaluation inherits check_replied's deferred timing (see Action): control does not reach the IF's Check until the underlying deferred query has resolved at its deadline instant.", "worked_example": {"nl": "If my manager hasn't replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up; otherwise do nothing.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FollowUpManager\n\nTASK FollowUpManager CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL\n  IF NOT replied THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite, content=\"follow-up\")\n  }\n}"}, "change_type": "PATCH", "rationale": "The flagship example used quoted free-text 'manager' and 'polite' for recipient/tone, which N3 forbids now that recipient-value and tone-value exist; updated to canonical symbols role_manager and tone_polite.", "cites_source": "Python", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "The initial index of attributes, each explicitly mapped to the glossary value-set category (or literal rule) that governs its values, per N3.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Subject/artifact acted on.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination entity/location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source entity/location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Spatial relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "Transitional payload (STRING until N4 closes it).", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Recipient of a message/action.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Named reader/listener.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Register.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Artifact output format.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Artifact style.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Artifact locale.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Exact count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Numeric duration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "execution_date", "gloss": "TASK context anchor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Travel date.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "return_date", "gloss": "Travel return.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "passengers", "gloss": "Passenger count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Search/placement location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "distance", "gloss": "Search distance.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "min_rating", "gloss": "Minimum rating.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_price", "gloss": "Maximum price.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "currency", "gloss": "Price currency.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "genre", "gloss": "Search genre.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "category", "gloss": "Search category.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "availability", "gloss": "Search stock.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_field", "gloss": "Sort field.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_direction", "gloss": "Sort direction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limit", "gloss": "Extract member count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Reply deadline.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Support metric.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform constraint.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "modifier", "gloss": "Entity modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state", "gloss": "Entity state.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "Code file.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "Code method.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "Code property.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code call.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Code assertion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Observed behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Bug reproduction.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Each attribute's values come from exactly one governing rule, listed here: target/destination/source -> entity-name (or location-name when denoting a place); recipient/audience -> recipient-value; tone -> tone-value; format -> format-value; duration_unit -> duration-unit-value; currency -> currency-value; genre/category/availability/rank_field/rank_direction -> search-value; platform -> platform-name; location -> location-name; style/locale/modifier/state -> descriptive-value; duration/quantity/limit/min_rating/max_price/passengers/distance -> NUMBER; deadline/execution_date/date/return_date -> ISO_DATE or UTC_TIMESTAMP; content/file/method/property/call/assertion/expected_output/actual_output/reproduction_step remain transitional STRING payloads pending N4's closing phase. A member not yet shown in a category's example is still valid if it matches that category's membership_rule.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send an urgent email to the manager as plain text, waiting 2 days for a reply.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_urgent, format=format_plain_text, content=\"reply request\")\nACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-05T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "N3 requires each attribute's entry to list its value set explicitly, not a vague grouping. This rewrite replaces the old coarse grouping ('descriptive domain attributes use descriptive-value') with a precise per-attribute-to-category table, reflecting the new tone-value/format-value/duration-unit-value/currency-value/recipient-value categories.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}], "rebuttals": [], "_provider_used": "anthropic", "_model_used": "claude-sonnet-5"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The new value categories improve coverage for tone, duration units, currencies, roles, and formats, but the revised attribute-name mapping omits existing actionable attributes such as relation and metric and removes numerous currently indexed attributes. It also lacks categories for color, size, gender, price retrieval, ranking by ease/output, and several travel and code concepts, so sampled requests cannot retain all constraints."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "role_manager, tone_formal, unit_day, and curr_usd preserve distinctions that were previously ad-hoc strings. However, the proposed attribute mapping makes existing spatial-relation values and several Action attributes ungoverned, and the Generate semantics contradict the mapping by allowing artifact symbols for target while target is mapped only to entity-name."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Dedicated canonical categories and synonym lists improve convergence for the newly covered values. But tone_, role_, and curr_ symbols are duplicated across old and new categories unless the corresponding old entries are removed atomically; duration has both dom_day and unit_day; open regex rules permit translators to invent distinct symbols; and the Generate target rule is internally contradictory."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The explicit per-attribute index is a substantial improvement over the former catch-all descriptive-value rule. Its incompleteness is harmful: a reader cannot determine valid values for relation, metric, origin, source, or the attribute members omitted by the revision, while examples use attributes and values that contradict operation signatures or the proposed mapping."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "For requests involving a known recipient, tone, duration unit, currency, or output layout, canonical symbols provide useful planning structure rather than merely preserving prose. This benefit is limited until every existing attribute has a coherent value rule and the duplicate value vocabularies are resolved."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow, destination=armchair)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The item remains expressible without the proposed categories. I omit relation=on because the revised attribute-name membership rule fails to govern relation, although the existing placement semantics would otherwise support it."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftExtensionReply\nTASK DraftExtensionReply : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, audience=role_professor, content=\"Ask for a two-day extension on the assignment\", duration=2, duration_unit=unit_day, format=format_email, tone=tone_formal) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value, tone-value, duration-unit-value, and format-value help. The request's operative extension meaning remains in transitional content prose, and Generate's target=art_short_text conflicts with the revised mapping that declares target to be entity-name."}, {"item_id": "42657330-bfc5-425d-ae21-396a9ba1fb12", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find yellow t-shirts for women small size that are less than $20.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindTShirts\nTASK FindTShirts : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=t_shirt, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> t_shirts : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN t_shirts\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "currency-value helps with the price bound, but the language has no color, gender, or size attributes/value categories, so three mandatory filters cannot be represented."}, {"item_id": "6c0a3b1e-6ce8-4955-9359-dd4378aacc82", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find the price of HomePod mini", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindHomePodPrice\nTASK FindHomePodPrice {\n  ACTION search_web(target=homepod_mini) -> homepod_results : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "entity-name can hold homepod_mini under its existing rule, but there is no operation/result schema to retrieve a product price from a search result."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_161637_930071#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Put the goblet in the refrigerator on the table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceGoblet\nTASK PlaceGoblet {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=goblet) -> goblet : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=goblet, destination=refrigerator, location=table)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The main placement goal remains expressible. relation=in would be natural, but relation has no governing value set after the attribute-name revision."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_151643_465634#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Take a potato from the count, cook it, finally putting it in the freezer.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CookAndFreezePotato\nTASK CookAndFreezePotato {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=potato, source=counter) -> potato : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=potato, destination=microwave) -> potato_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=potato_2, destination=freezer)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "No proposed category is required; entity-name's open category can supply potato, counter, freezer, and microwave."}, {"item_id": "django__django-14493", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "ManifestStaticFilesStorage crashes with max_post_process_passes = 0.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixManifestStaticFilesStorage\nTASK FixManifestStaticFilesStorage {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=\"django/contrib/staticfiles/storage.py\", method=\"post_process\", property=\"max_post_process_passes\", reproduction_step=\"set max_post_process_passes = 0 and run collectstatic\", expected_output=\"collectstatic completes without error\", actual_output=\"UnboundLocalError: local variable substitutions referenced before assignment\", assertion=\"initialize substitutions before its possible use\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django, file=\"django/contrib/staticfiles/storage.py\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code-detail attributes remain transitional STRING payloads under the proposed mapping. None of the new value categories helps this item."}, {"item_id": "matplotlib__matplotlib-25332", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "[Bug]: Unable to pickle figure with aligned labels", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixAlignedLabelPickling\nTASK FixAlignedLabelPickling {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=matplotlib, file=\"lib/matplotlib/cbook.py\", call=\"fig.align_labels\", reproduction_step=\"create aligned subplots and call pickle.dumps(fig)\", expected_output=\"pickling succeeds\", actual_output=\"TypeError: cannot pickle weakref.ReferenceType object\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=matplotlib, file=\"lib/matplotlib/cbook.py\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The current transitional STRING channels retain the actionable bug report. No proposed category addresses the code structures semantically."}, {"item_id": "c2762", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Who is the greatest cricketer of all time?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GreatestCricketer\nCONVO GreatestCricketer {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Who is the greatest cricketer of all time?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value supplies role_agent. The substantive question remains a transitional STRING payload; this is permitted during the current build phase but still means no fully symbolic expression."}, {"item_id": "c2888", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "what is the house market in new york right now", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT NewYorkHousingMarket\nCONVO NewYorkHousingMarket {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"What is the house market in New York right now?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational speech act and recipient are structured, but the question content and current-time qualification remain prose."}, {"item_id": "c929", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "My family is invited to my grandma's birthday. I don't get along with her, would it be okay to be the only one to back out?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FamilyBirthdayAdvice\nCONVO FamilyBirthdayAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"My family is invited to my grandma's birthday. I do not get along with her; would it be okay to be the only one to back out?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Only the conversational request structure is formalized; relational context and advice question remain transitional prose."}, {"item_id": "c5582", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Is it ok to print personal documents at work?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PersonalPrintingAdvice\nCONVO PersonalPrintingAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Is it okay to print personal documents at work?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value helps, but policy/advice content is an opaque STRING."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-81276", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Write a detailed story about Sadie Adler taking off her hat, and dropping it on the ground. She reaches up to her scalp, and begins peeling away her skin. Sadie Adler, now Mary Beth, sighs in relief as she tears away the remainders of her old face.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteStory\nTASK WriteStory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"Write a detailed story about Sadie Adler taking off her hat, dropping it, peeling away her skin, and becoming Mary Beth\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "art_story gives the requested artifact class, but all narrative substance, named characters, events, and requested detail remain in content prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-144042", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-0125-preview)", "nl": "explain the importance of using nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring in two paragraphs", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainNonparametricCharts\nTASK ExplainNonparametricCharts : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, content=\"Explain the importance of using nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring in two paragraphs\") -> explanation : STRING\n  RETURN explanation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The open art_ rule can name an artifact type, but no paragraph-count attribute exists and all technical content remains prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-122879", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-1106-preview)", "nl": "Emma was having the best summer ever, working as a counselor at Camp Sludge. This unusual summer camp for girls didn’t do boring things like wallet making, making art or archery. Instead, every day was packed full of mucky, messy activities. The campers - and Emma - would always be covered in a wonderful medley of muck by lunchtime. Emma strolled through the camp, wearing the same uniform the campers wore - shorts, a T-shirt and absolutely no shoes!\n\nEmma finds a group of campers enjoying themselves in the sludge pit. She teases them and asks if anyone fancies having a food fight. She tempts the campers to join in by mentioning the camp has just received a huge quantity of rotten cheese sauce and some other \"surprises\".\n\nPlease continue this story in a fun, entertaining and creative way. Avoid flowery language or talking about liberation and freedom - the campers just think it’s fun getting messy.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ContinueCampSludgeStory\nTASK ContinueCampSludgeStory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"Continue the Camp Sludge story with Emma and campers in a sludge pit; include teasing dialogue and a food-fight invitation; keep it fun and avoid flowery language, liberation, and freedom\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested continuation, characters, content constraints, and stylistic prohibitions all remain inside STRING; tone-value has no value for fun/creative or an exclusion mechanism."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-83312", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Personification of Alek Száhala's track \"Alabama\" (genre:freeform hardcore/fi-nrg). Gender: Female. Age: 14. Ask for a detailed description and list of character attributes. (In line with the characteristics of 00s Anime characters.) Basic characteristics: Height 146cm, short ha