Critic's decision: needs-rework
Critic's reasoning: The bundle makes substantive progress on N3 by introducing dedicated value categories and an explicit attribute-to-category index, but it cannot be accepted because doc hygiene fails and the index is incomplete and internally contradictory. It also regresses hard note N7 by creating duplicate canonical encodings for roles, tones, currencies, and day units. The standalone format-value category is self-contained and useful, but the remaining changes need an atomic, exhaustive migration and mapping revision.
Required changes (address every one explicitly): [{"target": "doc hygiene (scripted — blocks acceptance)", "change": "Doc hygiene FAILED — `Generate` missing glossary_gloss; `Flow-If` missing glossary_gloss"}, {"target": "basis", "change": "Fix the doc-hygiene failure: add glossary_gloss fields to the Generate and Flow-If revisions, so the revised glossary entries preserve their required glosses."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Replace the incomplete membership_rule with an exhaustive mapping for every attribute currently listed in the glossary and every attribute used by any Action, Generate, Utterance, Task CONTEXT, or worked example. At minimum add governing rules for relation, metric, origin, source, itinerary, route, travel_time, stop_count, policy, amenity, venue, showtime, ticket, seat, compatibility, revision, procedure, safety, escalation, academic_goal, job_search_goal, food, nutrition, meal, medical_topic, medical_audience, message_structure, and collaboration_structure; do not silently delete those current attributes."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Resolve the target contradiction explicitly: either map Generate.target to an artifact-value category while Action.target maps to entity-name, or split the attribute names by construct. The current global target -> entity-name rule conflicts with valid GENERATE(target=art_plan/art_story) examples and semantics."}, {"target": "descriptive-value", "change": "Make the vocabulary split atomic and non-overlapping. Remove or deprecate role_ and tone_ members from descriptive-value when recipient-value and tone-value become normative, remove curr_ from search-value when currency-value becomes normative, and define migration/canonicalization rules. Also remove dom_day or explicitly declare unit_day as its sole canonical replacement."}, {"target": "Generate", "change": "Align Generate's legal attributes and examples with the global attribute mapping and Action-style signatures. Define whether Generate may use target artifact symbols, and ensure every worked example is statically valid under that definition."}, {"target": "Action", "change": "Correct the tone-value worked example or the send_email signature: it currently uses format=format_plain_text even though send_email permits recipient, content, and optional tone only."}, {"target": "vocabulary basis", "change": "Add missing attribute categories needed by sampled closed tasks before restricting mappings: at least color, size, gender/audience demographic, product-price retrieval or price-result representation, construction difficulty, production/output/yield, and source/link request. Give each category canonical symbols and a deterministic membership rule."}, {"target": "format-value", "change": "Clarify its open membership rule: either every format_[a-z_]+ token is valid directly under the rule, or new layouts require prior glossary addition. The present statements say both, yielding contradictory validity criteria."}, {"target": "recipient-value", "change": "Preserve existing recipient coverage during the build phase by defining the permitted literal/category for named individual recipients, or explicitly retain the existing quoted recipient exception until a proper-name literal category is introduced. Do not make ordinary named recipients inexpressible."}]
Logic issues: ["Doc hygiene failed because the proposed Generate and Flow-If revisions omit glossary_gloss; this independently prevents acceptance.", "The attribute-name revision maps target to entity-name, but Generate semantics and every Generate example use art_ symbols from descriptive-value.", "The revision omits governing rules for existing relation and metric attributes and removes many existing attribute-name members, despite Action requiring every Action attribute to conform to a declared category/rule.", "send_email's declared signature does not allow format, but the tone-value worked example supplies format=format_plain_text.", "tone_, role_, and curr_ values have duplicate meanings across the newly added categories and their old categories; dom_day and unit_day provide two competing encodings for the same duration unit.", "format-value says arbitrary matching tokens are valid but also says layouts are valid only after being added as members; recipient-value has the same practical uncertainty for unlisted roles.", "The revised Flow-If worked example is improved for tone and recipient but still relies on deadline as a quoted UTC timestamp while the general value grammar does not independently define UTC_TIMESTAMP as a value literal form."]
Pre-KPI assessment: {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The new value categories improve coverage for tone, duration units, currencies, roles, and formats, but the revised attribute-name mapping omits existing actionable attributes such as relation and metric and removes numerous currently indexed attributes. It also lacks categories for color, size, gender, price retrieval, ranking by ease/output, and several travel and code concepts, so sampled requests cannot retain all constraints."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "role_manager, tone_formal, unit_day, and curr_usd preserve distinctions that were previously ad-hoc strings. However, the proposed attribute mapping makes existing spatial-relation values and several Action attributes ungoverned, and the Generate semantics contradict the mapping by allowing artifact symbols for target while target is mapped only to entity-name."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Dedicated canonical categories and synonym lists improve convergence for the newly covered values. But tone_, role_, and curr_ symbols are duplicated across old and new categories unless the corresponding old entries are removed atomically; duration has both dom_day and unit_day; open regex rules permit translators to invent distinct symbols; and the Generate target rule is internally contradictory."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "The explicit per-attribute index is a substantial improvement over the former catch-all descriptive-value rule. Its incompleteness is harmful: a reader cannot determine valid values for relation, metric, origin, source, or the attribute members omitted by the revision, while examples use attributes and values that contradict operation signatures or the proposed mapping."}, "improvement": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "For requests involving a known recipient, tone, duration unit, currency, or output layout, canonical symbols provide useful planning structure rather than merely preserving prose. This benefit is limited until every existing attribute has a coherent value rule and the duplicate value vocabularies are resolved."}}
Simulated examples that exposed gaps: [{"item_id": "dev-embodied-2", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Put both pillows from the sofa onto the armchair, one at a time.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MovePillows\nTASK MovePillows {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow, destination=armchair)\n  ACTION pick_up(target=pillow, source=sofa) -> pillow_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=pillow_2, destination=armchair)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The item remains expressible without the proposed categories. I omit relation=on because the revised attribute-name membership rule fails to govern relation, although the existing placement semantics would otherwise support it."}, {"item_id": "dev-email-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Draft a reply to my professor asking for a two-day extension on the assignment, and keep it formal.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DraftExtensionReply\nTASK DraftExtensionReply : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, audience=role_professor, content=\"Ask for a two-day extension on the assignment\", duration=2, duration_unit=unit_day, format=format_email, tone=tone_formal) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value, tone-value, duration-unit-value, and format-value help. The request's operative extension meaning remains in transitional content prose, and Generate's target=art_short_text conflicts with the revised mapping that declares target to be entity-name."}, {"item_id": "42657330-bfc5-425d-ae21-396a9ba1fb12", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find yellow t-shirts for women small size that are less than $20.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindTShirts\nTASK FindTShirts : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=t_shirt, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> t_shirts : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN t_shirts\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "currency-value helps with the price bound, but the language has no color, gender, or size attributes/value categories, so three mandatory filters cannot be represented."}, {"item_id": "6c0a3b1e-6ce8-4955-9359-dd4378aacc82", "source": "Mind2Web (osunlp/Mind2Web, train, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Find the price of HomePod mini", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindHomePodPrice\nTASK FindHomePodPrice {\n  ACTION search_web(target=homepod_mini) -> homepod_results : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "entity-name can hold homepod_mini under its existing rule, but there is no operation/result schema to retrieve a product price from a search result."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_161637_930071#1", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Put the goblet in the refrigerator on the table.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlaceGoblet\nTASK PlaceGoblet {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=goblet) -> goblet : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=goblet, destination=refrigerator, location=table)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The main placement goal remains expressible. relation=in would be natural, but relation has no governing value set after the attribute-name revision."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_151643_465634#2", "source": "ALFRED (json_2.1.0, train)", "nl": "Take a potato from the count, cook it, finally putting it in the freezer.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT CookAndFreezePotato\nTASK CookAndFreezePotato {\n  ACTION pick_up(target=potato, source=counter) -> potato : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION heat(target=potato, destination=microwave) -> potato_2 : REF[STRING]\n  ACTION place(target=potato_2, destination=freezer)\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "No proposed category is required; entity-name's open category can supply potato, counter, freezer, and microwave."}, {"item_id": "django__django-14493", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "ManifestStaticFilesStorage crashes with max_post_process_passes = 0.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixManifestStaticFilesStorage\nTASK FixManifestStaticFilesStorage {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=django, file=\"django/contrib/staticfiles/storage.py\", method=\"post_process\", property=\"max_post_process_passes\", reproduction_step=\"set max_post_process_passes = 0 and run collectstatic\", expected_output=\"collectstatic completes without error\", actual_output=\"UnboundLocalError: local variable substitutions referenced before assignment\", assertion=\"initialize substitutions before its possible use\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=django, file=\"django/contrib/staticfiles/storage.py\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The code-detail attributes remain transitional STRING payloads under the proposed mapping. None of the new value categories helps this item."}, {"item_id": "matplotlib__matplotlib-25332", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified (princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Verified, test, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "[Bug]: Unable to pickle figure with aligned labels", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixAlignedLabelPickling\nTASK FixAlignedLabelPickling {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=matplotlib, file=\"lib/matplotlib/cbook.py\", call=\"fig.align_labels\", reproduction_step=\"create aligned subplots and call pickle.dumps(fig)\", expected_output=\"pickling succeeds\", actual_output=\"TypeError: cannot pickle weakref.ReferenceType object\")\n  ACTION run_tests(target=matplotlib, file=\"lib/matplotlib/cbook.py\")\n}", "coverage": "Full", "notes": "The current transitional STRING channels retain the actionable bug report. No proposed category addresses the code structures semantically."}, {"item_id": "c2762", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Who is the greatest cricketer of all time?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GreatestCricketer\nCONVO GreatestCricketer {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Who is the greatest cricketer of all time?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value supplies role_agent. The substantive question remains a transitional STRING payload; this is permitted during the current build phase but still means no fully symbolic expression."}, {"item_id": "c2888", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "what is the house market in new york right now", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT NewYorkHousingMarket\nCONVO NewYorkHousingMarket {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"What is the house market in New York right now?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The conversational speech act and recipient are structured, but the question content and current-time qualification remain prose."}, {"item_id": "c929", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "My family is invited to my grandma's birthday. I don't get along with her, would it be okay to be the only one to back out?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FamilyBirthdayAdvice\nCONVO FamilyBirthdayAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"My family is invited to my grandma's birthday. I do not get along with her; would it be okay to be the only one to back out?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Only the conversational request structure is formalized; relational context and advice question remain transitional prose."}, {"item_id": "c5582", "source": "PRISM (HannahRoseKirk/prism-alignment, conversations config, Parquet column-projected sample)", "nl": "Is it ok to print personal documents at work?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PersonalPrintingAdvice\nCONVO PersonalPrintingAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Is it okay to print personal documents at work?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value helps, but policy/advice content is an opaque STRING."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-81276", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Write a detailed story about Sadie Adler taking off her hat, and dropping it on the ground. She reaches up to her scalp, and begins peeling away her skin. Sadie Adler, now Mary Beth, sighs in relief as she tears away the remainders of her old face.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WriteStory\nTASK WriteStory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"Write a detailed story about Sadie Adler taking off her hat, dropping it, peeling away her skin, and becoming Mary Beth\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "art_story gives the requested artifact class, but all narrative substance, named characters, events, and requested detail remain in content prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-144042", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-0125-preview)", "nl": "explain the importance of using nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring in two paragraphs", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ExplainNonparametricCharts\nTASK ExplainNonparametricCharts : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, content=\"Explain the importance of using nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring in two paragraphs\") -> explanation : STRING\n  RETURN explanation\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The open art_ rule can name an artifact type, but no paragraph-count attribute exists and all technical content remains prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-122879", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-4-1106-preview)", "nl": "Emma was having the best summer ever, working as a counselor at Camp Sludge. This unusual summer camp for girls didn’t do boring things like wallet making, making art or archery. Instead, every day was packed full of mucky, messy activities. The campers - and Emma - would always be covered in a wonderful medley of muck by lunchtime. Emma strolled through the camp, wearing the same uniform the campers wore - shorts, a T-shirt and absolutely no shoes!\n\nEmma finds a group of campers enjoying themselves in the sludge pit. She teases them and asks if anyone fancies having a food fight. She tempts the campers to join in by mentioning the camp has just received a huge quantity of rotten cheese sauce and some other \"surprises\".\n\nPlease continue this story in a fun, entertaining and creative way. Avoid flowery language or talking about liberation and freedom - the campers just think it’s fun getting messy.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ContinueCampSludgeStory\nTASK ContinueCampSludgeStory : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_story, content=\"Continue the Camp Sludge story with Emma and campers in a sludge pit; include teasing dialogue and a food-fight invitation; keep it fun and avoid flowery language, liberation, and freedom\") -> story : STRING\n  RETURN story\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The requested continuation, characters, content constraints, and stylistic prohibitions all remain inside STRING; tone-value has no value for fun/creative or an exclusion mechanism."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-83312", "source": "PATHs (microsoft/prototypical-hai-collaborations, wildchat1m_en3u-task_utterance_wintent_anns, model=gpt-3.5-turbo-0613)", "nl": "Personification of Alek Száhala's track \"Alabama\" (genre:freeform hardcore/fi-nrg). Gender: Female. Age: 14. Ask for a detailed description and list of character attributes. (In line with the characteristics of 00s Anime characters.) Basic characteristics: Height 146cm, short hair, Dark blue pupils and hair, quiet and sentimental, gray dress, loli, etc.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT DescribeAlabamaCharacter\nTASK DescribeAlabamaCharacter : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_character_profile, content=\"Create a detailed 00s-anime character description and attribute list personifying Alek Szahala's track Alabama: female, age 14, height 146 cm, short dark-blue hair and pupils, quiet, sentimental, gray dress\") -> character_profile : STRING\n  RETURN character_profile\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The artifact can be represented through the art_ category, but identity, genre, gender, age, height, appearance, personality, and list requirement lack structured categories and remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775857728160", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Search the best and the easiests creeper farms that are efortless to build and provide me a lot of gunpowder", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FindCreeperFarms\nTASK FindCreeperFarms : LIST[REF[STRING]] {\n  ACTION search_web(target=creeper_farm) -> farms : LIST[REF[STRING]]\n  RETURN farms\n}", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The target can use entity-name's open rule, but no attributes/categories express easy construction, high gunpowder output, ranking over both criteria, or the implied request for sources/links."}, {"item_id": "1775488035768", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "Hi! How to join the military engineering school", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MilitaryEngineeringSchool\nCONVO MilitaryEngineeringSchool {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"How do I join military engineering school?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request is represented as a conversational question with a canonical recipient, while the educational/career substance remains a STRING."}, {"item_id": "1773875884407", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "hello, i wanna plan a trip to morroco", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanMoroccoTrip\nTASK PlanMoroccoTrip : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a trip to Morocco\") -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "art_plan gives a structured output intent, but Morocco and all itinerary content are in transitional prose; no travel-destination attribute governs this use."}, {"item_id": "1775494752255", "source": "ThoughtTrace (SCAI-JHU/ThoughtTrace, Parquet column-projected sample, JSON-decoded messages)", "nl": "hello", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"hello\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The speech act and intended recipient are structured, but greeting content remains a transitional STRING payload."}]
