**Introduced/last revised:** sprint 17, see `changelog.md#sprint-17`

### `descriptive-value` (vocabulary)

**Gloss:** A unified category for roles, tones, artifacts, modifiers, states, and domain concepts.

**Category:** open — the members below are representative

**Members:**
- `role_user` — The requesting human.
- `role_agent` — The assistant.
- `role_manager` — The user's manager.
- `tone_polite` — Courteous.
- `tone_casual` — Informal.
- `tone_concise` — Brief.
- `art_story` — Narrative story.
- `art_short_text` — Short text.
- `art_plan` — Actionable plan.
- `art_structured_report` — Headed report.
- `mod_mixed_case` — Mixed case modifier.
- `state_microwaved` — Microwaved state.
- `dom_safari` — Safari concept.
- `dom_pain` — Pain concept.
- `dom_ovr` — One-vs-rest concept.
- `dom_sgi` — SGI concept.
- `dom_day` — Day unit.

**Membership rule:** A unified category for roles, tones, artifacts, modifiers, states, and domain concepts. Members are prefixed: `role_`, `tone_`, `art_`, `mod_`, `state_`, `dom_`. The suffix is an atomic `[a-z_]+` string. Added to satisfy the need for descriptive categories within the 12-change limit.

**Example:**
- NL: "Plan a 3 day safari."
- BrainCode: `GENERATE(target=art_plan, content="Plan a safari", duration=3, duration_unit=dom_day) -> plan : STRING`

**Introduced/last revised:** sprint 17, see `changelog.md#sprint-17`

### `format-value` (vocabulary)

**Gloss:** Canonical output-format symbols for the format attribute (used by GENERATE and message-producing Actions/Utterances).

**Category:** open — the members below are representative

**Members:**
- `format_plain_text` — Unstructured prose text. (natural-language synonyms: plain text)
- `format_bullet_list` — Bulleted list. (natural-language synonyms: bullet points, bulleted)
- `format_numbered_list` — Numbered list. (natural-language synonyms: numbered steps)
- `format_email` — Email message layout. (natural-language synonyms: as an email)
- `format_markdown` — Markdown-formatted text. (natural-language synonyms: in markdown)
- `format_table` — Tabular layout. (natural-language synonyms: as a table)
- `format_pdf` — PDF document. (natural-language synonyms: as a pdf)

**Membership rule:** An atomic symbol matching `format_[a-z_]+` naming a concrete output layout. New layouts are added as new members, never as free text.

**Example:**
- NL: "Give me the steps as a numbered list."
- BrainCode: `GENERATE(target=art_plan, content="steps", format=format_numbered_list) -> plan : STRING`

**Introduced/last revised:** sprint 18, see `changelog.md#sprint-18`


Proposed changes available for this translation:
- [revise] Generate: grammar `generation ::= "GENERATE" "(" generate-attr ("," generate-attr)* ")" "->" IDENT ":" gen_type
generate-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
gen_type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" gen_type"]"` — Only target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes. target's value is an artifact-value symbol (GENERATE always produces an artifact, never an entity, so target is governed by artifact-value, distinct from Action's entity-name-governed target). audience is governed by recipient-value. tone is governed by tone-value. format is governed by format-value. duration_unit is governed by duration-unit-value. duration and quantity are NUMBER. style and locale remain governed by descriptive-value. Canonical ordering rule: attributes emitted in exactly declared signature order (target first, then optional attributes alphabetically). Handle rule: bound IDENT reflects the target artifact's normalized noun; collisions get `_2`, `_3` in source order. content remains a transitional STRING channel pending N4's closing phase.
- [revise] Flow-If: grammar `flow_if ::= "IF" check "THEN" "{" step+ "}" ( "ELSE" "{" step+ "}" )?` — Conditional branching, used identically inside TASK and CONVO TURN bodies. The Check is evaluated first, at the moment control reaches the IF. If true, THEN's steps execute in order; if false and ELSE is present, its steps execute instead; if false with no ELSE, control passes to the following step. Flow-If may nest inside another Flow-If or a FOR-EACH body; nested Checks evaluate only when control actually reaches them. THEN and ELSE each open a fresh child scope: a binding inside THEN is invisible in ELSE, after the IF, or to siblings, and vice versa. An IF nested inside a TURN body may contain UTTER in its branches exactly as it may contain ACTION; the same nesting inside a TASK body remains a static error per Utterance's restriction. When a Check depends on a preceding `check_replied` with a future `deadline`, the branch inherits that deferred timing.
- [add vocabulary] tone-value (closed): The closed set of register/tone symbols usable wherever an attribute calls for a tone (Action's tone, UTTER's tone, GENERATE's tone). Members: tone_polite, tone_formal, tone_casual, tone_concise, tone_neutral, tone_urgent, tone_empathetic, tone_professional
- [add vocabulary] duration-unit-value (closed): The closed set of time units usable with the duration_unit attribute. Members: unit_second, unit_minute, unit_hour, unit_day, unit_week, unit_month, unit_year
- [add vocabulary] currency-value (open): Canonical currency-code symbols for the currency attribute, used with price bounds in search and generation. Members: curr_usd, curr_eur, curr_gbp, curr_jpy, curr_ils; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `curr_[a-z]{3}` naming an ISO-4217-style currency code. This is now the sole canonical location for currency symbols; search-value no longer carries curr_ members.
- [add vocabulary] recipient-value (open): Canonical role/recipient symbols for the recipient and audience attributes. Members: role_user, role_agent, role_manager, role_professor, role_friend, role_colleague, role_support_team, role_customer; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `role_[a-z_]+` naming a person-role, class, or audience type. For a specific named individual not covered by any role symbol (e.g. a personal name like 'John'), a quoted STRING remains a transitional exception — exactly as entity-name allows for physical objects — pending a dedicated proper-name literal category under N5; a role_ symbol must be used instead whenever one applies. This preserves existing coverage of named recipients rather than making them inexpressible.
- [add vocabulary] artifact-value (open): The canonical set of generated-artifact-type symbols usable as GENERATE's target attribute. Members: art_story, art_short_text, art_plan, art_structured_report, art_technical_explanation, art_character_profile; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `art_[a-z_]+` naming a class of generated artifact (document type, narrative form, structured output). Per N6, assume the complete glossary already contains the needed artifact member for a given request; a genuinely new artifact type is added as a new member in a future sprint, never expressed as free text.
- [revise vocabulary] descriptive-value (open): A residual, still-open category for entity modifiers, entity states, and unclassified domain concepts not yet covered by a dedicated attribute-value category (roles, tones, currencies, artifact types, and durations now have their own categories and must not be duplicated here). Members: mod_mixed_case, state_microwaved, dom_safari, dom_pain, dom_ovr, dom_sgi; membership rule: A residual bucket for entity-modifier (`mod_`), entity-state (`state_`), and unclassified domain-concept (`dom_`) symbols. role_, tone_, curr_, art_, and unit_ symbols are retired from this category — use recipient-value, tone-value, currency-value, artifact-value, and duration-unit-value respectively instead; dom_day is retired in favor of unit_day.
- [revise vocabulary] search-value (open): Canonical namespaced values for ranking, sort-direction, genre, category, and availability attributes (currency now lives exclusively in currency-value). Members: rank_price, rank_rating, rank_distance, dir_asc, dir_desc, cat_game, cat_limited_time_offers, avail_in_stock, avail_out_of_stock, genre_comedy; membership rule: Members are prefixed by `rank_`, `dir_`, `genre_`, `cat_`, `avail_`, each an atomic `[a-z_]+` suffix. Currency no longer belongs here; use currency-value.
