   "user (None, score=None): sit did kind of seem like you had an opinion. So, for me - in New Zealand the native people, the Maori were part of the process of migrants coming from the UK, Ireland etc. A treaty was formed. Then in the mid 1980's the maori population started causing issues, they were taken advantage of etc.... ultimately ending in hundreds of settlement awards going out from the crown to the maori tribes (this from 1980 - present). However, it has not ended there, more focus in healthcare has been given to the one group of people, more preference, different rules surrounding education - all in an effort to appease the people making the most noise. So, now that  our entire society has given up so much, paid the maori out, we are still being subject to more and more and more ludicrous requests. So, now in New Zealand it feels like white people are not being targeted racially rather than Maori. As we are the disadvantaged now",
