Shaper proposal: {"summary": "Fixes doc-hygiene (added glossary_glosses), resolves the target-attribute contradiction by splitting artifact-value out from descriptive-value, de-duplicates tone/role/currency symbols across categories, gives attribute-name a complete per-attribute mapping (including previously-omitted attributes), and adds a product-attribute-value category as a first step on color/size/gender coverage.", "note_position": "comply", "note_argument": "Every attribute touched now resolves to exactly one glossary-defined value category (or an explicitly-tracked transitional STRING gap, never silent free text), satisfying N3's build-phase requirement without duplicating canonical symbols across categories.", "foundations_overview": null, "rebuttals": [], "changes": [{"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Generate", "grammar": "generation ::= \"GENERATE\" \"(\" generate-attr (\",\" generate-attr)* \")\" \"->\" IDENT \":\" gen_type\ngenerate-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\ngen_type ::= \"NUMBER\" | \"STRING\" | \"BOOL\" | \"LIST\" \"[\" gen_type\"]\"", "semantics": "Only target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, and tone are legal Generate attributes. target's value is an artifact-value symbol (GENERATE always produces an artifact, never an entity, so target is governed by artifact-value, distinct from Action's entity-name-governed target). audience is governed by recipient-value. tone is governed by tone-value. format is governed by format-value. duration_unit is governed by duration-unit-value. duration and quantity are NUMBER. style and locale remain governed by descriptive-value. Canonical ordering rule: attributes emitted in exactly declared signature order (target first, then optional attributes alphabetically). Handle rule: bound IDENT reflects the target artifact's normalized noun; collisions get `_2`, `_3` in source order. content remains a transitional STRING channel pending N4's closing phase.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3 day safari.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PlanSafari\nTASK PlanSafari : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day) -> plan : STRING\n  RETURN plan\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "GENERATE produces a non-effectful artifact (a plan, story, report, etc.); its target names the kind of artifact from the artifact-value category, and its other attributes (tone, format, duration_unit, audience) each draw from their own dedicated value category.", "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Resolves the Critic's target contradiction directly: Generate.target is now explicitly artifact-value (not entity-name), matching every one of its own worked examples, while Action.target stays entity-name via the separate Action signature list.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "construct_name": "Flow-If", "grammar": "flow_if ::= \"IF\" check \"THEN\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" ( \"ELSE\" \"{\" step+ \"}\" )?", "semantics": "Conditional branching, used identically inside TASK and CONVO TURN bodies. The Check is evaluated first, at the moment control reaches the IF. If true, THEN's steps execute in order; if false and ELSE is present, its steps execute instead; if false with no ELSE, control passes to the following step. Flow-If may nest inside another Flow-If or a FOR-EACH body; nested Checks evaluate only when control actually reaches them. THEN and ELSE each open a fresh child scope: a binding inside THEN is invisible in ELSE, after the IF, or to siblings, and vice versa. An IF nested inside a TURN body may contain UTTER in its branches exactly as it may contain ACTION; the same nesting inside a TASK body remains a static error per Utterance's restriction. When a Check depends on a preceding `check_replied` with a future `deadline`, the branch inherits that deferred timing.", "worked_example": {"nl": "If my manager hasn't replied by Friday, send a polite follow-up; otherwise do nothing.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FollowUpManager\n\nTASK FollowUpManager CONTEXT execution_date=\"2025-06-03\" {\n  ACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL\n  IF NOT replied THEN {\n    ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite, content=\"follow-up\")\n  }\n}"}, "glossary_gloss": "Flow-If lets a task branch on a Check: it runs the THEN block if the Check is true, otherwise the optional ELSE block, each in its own fresh variable scope, and works identically inside Task bodies and conversation Turn bodies.", "change_type": "PATCH", "rationale": "Restores the required glossary_gloss (doc-hygiene failure) and keeps the worked example on canonical role_manager/tone_polite symbols now that recipient-value and tone-value exist.", "cites_source": null, "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "tone-value", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of register/tone symbols usable wherever an attribute calls for a tone (Action's tone, UTTER's tone, GENERATE's tone).", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "tone_polite", "gloss": "Courteous, respectful register.", "nl_synonyms": ["politely", "kindly"]}, {"symbol": "tone_formal", "gloss": "Formal register.", "nl_synonyms": ["formally"]}, {"symbol": "tone_casual", "gloss": "Informal register.", "nl_synonyms": ["casually"]}, {"symbol": "tone_concise", "gloss": "Brief, to-the-point register.", "nl_synonyms": ["briefly", "concisely"]}, {"symbol": "tone_neutral", "gloss": "Plain, unmarked register.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone_urgent", "gloss": "Conveys urgency.", "nl_synonyms": ["urgently", "ASAP"]}, {"symbol": "tone_empathetic", "gloss": "Conveys empathy/understanding.", "nl_synonyms": ["sympathetically"]}, {"symbol": "tone_professional", "gloss": "Workplace-appropriate register.", "nl_synonyms": ["professionally"]}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Send an urgent email to the manager.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_urgent, content=\"status update request\")"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "tone previously accepted transitional quoted strings with no defined value set, violating N3. A closed enum matches the Python Enum precedent for deterministic configuration values.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "duration-unit-value", "glossary_gloss": "The closed set of time units usable with the duration_unit attribute.", "closed": true, "members": [{"symbol": "unit_second", "gloss": "Seconds.", "nl_synonyms": ["seconds", "sec"]}, {"symbol": "unit_minute", "gloss": "Minutes.", "nl_synonyms": ["minutes", "min"]}, {"symbol": "unit_hour", "gloss": "Hours.", "nl_synonyms": ["hours"]}, {"symbol": "unit_day", "gloss": "Days.", "nl_synonyms": ["days"]}, {"symbol": "unit_week", "gloss": "Weeks.", "nl_synonyms": ["weeks"]}, {"symbol": "unit_month", "gloss": "Months.", "nl_synonyms": ["months"]}, {"symbol": "unit_year", "gloss": "Years.", "nl_synonyms": ["years"]}], "membership_rule": null, "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a 3 day safari.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", duration=3, duration_unit=unit_day) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "duration_unit previously borrowed dom_day from the catch-all descriptive-value bucket; a dedicated closed category composes cleanly with NUMBER for duration and is the sole canonical encoding (dom_day is retired, see descriptive-value revision).", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "currency-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical currency-code symbols for the currency attribute, used with price bounds in search and generation.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "curr_usd", "gloss": "United States dollar.", "nl_synonyms": ["$", "usd", "dollars"]}, {"symbol": "curr_eur", "gloss": "Euro.", "nl_synonyms": ["eur", "euros"]}, {"symbol": "curr_gbp", "gloss": "British pound.", "nl_synonyms": ["gbp", "pounds"]}, {"symbol": "curr_jpy", "gloss": "Japanese yen.", "nl_synonyms": ["jpy", "yen"]}, {"symbol": "curr_ils", "gloss": "Israeli new shekel.", "nl_synonyms": ["ils", "shekels"]}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `curr_[a-z]{3}` naming an ISO-4217-style currency code. This is now the sole canonical location for currency symbols; search-value no longer carries curr_ members.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the cheapest mirror under 20 euros.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, currency=curr_eur, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "currency is its own attribute (used outside search too) and deserves its own traceable entry per N3; consolidating removes the curr_usd duplicate that previously lived in search-value.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "recipient-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical role/recipient symbols for the recipient and audience attributes.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "role_user", "gloss": "The requesting human.", "nl_synonyms": ["me", "I"]}, {"symbol": "role_agent", "gloss": "The assistant.", "nl_synonyms": ["you", "the assistant"]}, {"symbol": "role_manager", "gloss": "The user's manager.", "nl_synonyms": ["my manager", "boss"]}, {"symbol": "role_professor", "gloss": "The user's professor/instructor.", "nl_synonyms": ["my professor", "teacher"]}, {"symbol": "role_friend", "gloss": "A friend of the user.", "nl_synonyms": ["my friend"]}, {"symbol": "role_colleague", "gloss": "A coworker of the user.", "nl_synonyms": ["my colleague", "coworker"]}, {"symbol": "role_support_team", "gloss": "A customer-support team.", "nl_synonyms": ["support", "customer service"]}, {"symbol": "role_customer", "gloss": "A customer/client of the user.", "nl_synonyms": ["the customer", "client"]}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `role_[a-z_]+` naming a person-role, class, or audience type. For a specific named individual not covered by any role symbol (e.g. a personal name like 'John'), a quoted STRING remains a transitional exception — exactly as entity-name allows for physical objects — pending a dedicated proper-name literal category under N5; a role_ symbol must be used instead whenever one applies. This preserves existing coverage of named recipients rather than making them inexpressible.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send an urgent email to the manager.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_urgent, content=\"status update request\")"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "recipient/audience previously used quoted strings with no value set; role_ symbols already existed scattered in descriptive-value but were not indexed as their own attribute-scoped category. The explicit transitional-STRING clause answers the Critic's coverage-regression concern for named individuals.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "artifact-value", "glossary_gloss": "The canonical set of generated-artifact-type symbols usable as GENERATE's target attribute.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "art_story", "gloss": "Narrative story.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_short_text", "gloss": "Short free text.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_plan", "gloss": "Actionable plan.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_structured_report", "gloss": "Headed/structured report.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_technical_explanation", "gloss": "Technical explanation of a concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "art_character_profile", "gloss": "Descriptive character profile.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `art_[a-z_]+` naming a class of generated artifact (document type, narrative form, structured output). Per N6, assume the complete glossary already contains the needed artifact member for a given request; a genuinely new artifact type is added as a new member in a future sprint, never expressed as free text.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Explain the importance of nonparametric control charts.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_technical_explanation, content=\"Explain the importance of nonparametric control charts for process mean and variability monitoring\") -> explanation : STRING"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Splits the artifact-type symbols out of the mixed descriptive-value bucket into their own attribute-scoped category, resolving the Critic's target contradiction (Generate.target now maps here, not to entity-name).", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "descriptive-value", "glossary_gloss": "A residual, still-open category for entity modifiers, entity states, and unclassified domain concepts not yet covered by a dedicated attribute-value category (roles, tones, currencies, artifact types, and durations now have their own categories and must not be duplicated here).", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "mod_mixed_case", "gloss": "Mixed case modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state_microwaved", "gloss": "Microwaved state.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_safari", "gloss": "Safari concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_pain", "gloss": "Pain concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_ovr", "gloss": "One-vs-rest concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "dom_sgi", "gloss": "SGI concept.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "A residual bucket for entity-modifier (`mod_`), entity-state (`state_`), and unclassified domain-concept (`dom_`) symbols. role_, tone_, curr_, art_, and unit_ symbols are retired from this category — use recipient-value, tone-value, currency-value, artifact-value, and duration-unit-value respectively instead; dom_day is retired in favor of unit_day.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Plan a safari.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"Plan a safari\", style=dom_safari) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Removes the duplicate canonical encodings (role_, tone_, curr_, art_, dom_day) that the Critic flagged as an N7 determinism regression, leaving one and only one category per concern.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "search-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical namespaced values for ranking, sort-direction, genre, category, and availability attributes (currency now lives exclusively in currency-value).", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "rank_price", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: monetary cost.", "nl_synonyms": ["cheapest", "lowest price"]}, {"symbol": "rank_rating", "gloss": "Rank or filter field: user or critic score.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_distance", "gloss": "Rank field: proximity.", "nl_synonyms": ["nearest", "closest"]}, {"symbol": "dir_asc", "gloss": "Ascending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["lowest first"]}, {"symbol": "dir_desc", "gloss": "Descending rank direction.", "nl_synonyms": ["highest first"]}, {"symbol": "cat_game", "gloss": "Category: video game.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "cat_limited_time_offers", "gloss": "Category: time-limited deals.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "avail_in_stock", "gloss": "Available for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["available"]}, {"symbol": "avail_out_of_stock", "gloss": "Unavailable for purchase now.", "nl_synonyms": ["sold out"]}, {"symbol": "genre_comedy", "gloss": "Genre: comedy.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Members are prefixed by `rank_`, `dir_`, `genre_`, `cat_`, `avail_`, each an atomic `[a-z_]+` suffix. Currency no longer belongs here; use currency-value.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find the highest-rated in-stock comedy game.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=game, genre=genre_comedy, category=cat_game, availability=avail_in_stock) -> games : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=games, rank_field=rank_rating, rank_direction=dir_desc) -> sorted_games : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Removing curr_usd here eliminates its duplicate with currency-value, fixing the N7 determinism regression the Critic flagged.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "format-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical output-format symbols for the format attribute (used by GENERATE and message-producing Actions/Utterances).", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "format_plain_text", "gloss": "Unstructured prose text.", "nl_synonyms": ["plain text"]}, {"symbol": "format_bullet_list", "gloss": "Bulleted list.", "nl_synonyms": ["bullet points", "bulleted"]}, {"symbol": "format_numbered_list", "gloss": "Numbered list.", "nl_synonyms": ["numbered steps"]}, {"symbol": "format_email", "gloss": "Email message layout.", "nl_synonyms": ["as an email"]}, {"symbol": "format_markdown", "gloss": "Markdown-formatted text.", "nl_synonyms": ["in markdown"]}, {"symbol": "format_table", "gloss": "Tabular layout.", "nl_synonyms": ["as a table"]}, {"symbol": "format_pdf", "gloss": "PDF document.", "nl_synonyms": ["as a pdf"]}], "membership_rule": "A translator must use an existing member whenever one fits the requested layout. Only when no member fits may a translator mint a new atomic `format_[a-z_]+` symbol following this pattern (per N6, assume the complete glossary already lists the needed layout); that new symbol is then recorded as a glossary member in the next sprint. No free-text format description is ever permitted, regardless of whether a member currently exists.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Give me the steps as a numbered list.", "braincode": "GENERATE(target=art_plan, content=\"steps\", format=format_numbered_list) -> plan : STRING"}, "change_type": "PATCH", "rationale": "Resolves the Critic-flagged contradiction between 'any format_[a-z_]+ token is valid' and 'new layouts require prior addition' by stating the single rule other open categories already follow: prefer an existing member, mint atomically only as a last resort, never free text.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "add", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "product-attribute-value", "glossary_gloss": "Canonical color, size, and gender/demographic-audience symbols for product search and filtering attributes.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "color_yellow", "gloss": "Yellow.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color_red", "gloss": "Red.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color_black", "gloss": "Black.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color_white", "gloss": "White.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size_small", "gloss": "Small size.", "nl_synonyms": ["small", "S"]}, {"symbol": "size_medium", "gloss": "Medium size.", "nl_synonyms": ["medium", "M"]}, {"symbol": "size_large", "gloss": "Large size.", "nl_synonyms": ["large", "L"]}, {"symbol": "gender_women", "gloss": "Women's/female-targeted.", "nl_synonyms": ["women", "female"]}, {"symbol": "gender_men", "gloss": "Men's/male-targeted.", "nl_synonyms": ["men", "male"]}, {"symbol": "gender_unisex", "gloss": "Unisex.", "nl_synonyms": ["unisex"]}], "membership_rule": "An atomic symbol matching `(color|size|gender)_[a-z_]+` naming a product color, garment/item size, or demographic-audience facet. New values are added as new members following this prefix pattern, never as free text.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Find yellow t-shirts for women, small size, under $20.", "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=t_shirt, color=color_yellow, size=size_small, gender=gender_women, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> t_shirts : LIST[REF[STRING]]"}, "change_type": "MINOR", "rationale": "Begins closing the Critic-flagged vocab-basis gap (no color/size/gender categories). This sprint adds the value category; wiring color/size/gender into search_web's Action signature is a small, separate follow-up tracked for next sprint so as to stay within the 12-change scope limit without leaving the symbols undefined in the meantime.", "addresses_note": "N3"}, {"op": "revise", "kind": "vocabulary", "construct_name": "attribute-name", "glossary_gloss": "The complete index of attributes, each mapped to the exact glossary value-set category, literal rule, or explicitly-tracked transitional STRING channel that governs its values, per N3.", "closed": false, "members": [{"symbol": "target", "gloss": "Subject/artifact acted on or generated.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "destination", "gloss": "Destination entity/location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "source", "gloss": "Source entity/location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "relation", "gloss": "Spatial relation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "content", "gloss": "Transitional payload (STRING until N4 closes it).", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "recipient", "gloss": "Recipient of a message/action.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "audience", "gloss": "Named reader/listener of a generated artifact.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "tone", "gloss": "Register.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "format", "gloss": "Artifact output format.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "style", "gloss": "Artifact style.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "locale", "gloss": "Artifact locale.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "quantity", "gloss": "Exact count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration", "gloss": "Numeric duration.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "duration_unit", "gloss": "Duration unit.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "execution_date", "gloss": "TASK context anchor.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "origin", "gloss": "Travel origin.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "date", "gloss": "Travel date.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "return_date", "gloss": "Travel return.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "passengers", "gloss": "Passenger count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "location", "gloss": "Search/placement location.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "distance", "gloss": "Search distance.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "min_rating", "gloss": "Minimum rating.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "max_price", "gloss": "Maximum price.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "currency", "gloss": "Price currency.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "genre", "gloss": "Search genre.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "category", "gloss": "Search category.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "availability", "gloss": "Search stock.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_field", "gloss": "Sort field.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "rank_direction", "gloss": "Sort direction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "limit", "gloss": "Extract member count.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "deadline", "gloss": "Reply deadline.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "metric", "gloss": "Support metric.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "platform", "gloss": "Platform constraint.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "modifier", "gloss": "Entity modifier.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "state", "gloss": "Entity state.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "itinerary", "gloss": "Travel itinerary.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "route", "gloss": "Travel route.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "travel_time", "gloss": "Travel time.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "stop_count", "gloss": "Transit stops.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "policy", "gloss": "Policy.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "amenity", "gloss": "Amenity.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "venue", "gloss": "Venue.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "showtime", "gloss": "Showtime.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "ticket", "gloss": "Ticket.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "seat", "gloss": "Seat.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "compatibility", "gloss": "Compatibility.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "file", "gloss": "Code file.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "method", "gloss": "Code method.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "property", "gloss": "Code property.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "call", "gloss": "Code call.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "assertion", "gloss": "Code assertion.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "expected_output", "gloss": "Expected behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "actual_output", "gloss": "Observed behavior.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "reproduction_step", "gloss": "Bug reproduction.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "revision", "gloss": "Revision.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "procedure", "gloss": "Procedure.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "safety", "gloss": "Safety.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "escalation", "gloss": "Escalation.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "academic_goal", "gloss": "Academic goal.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "job_search_goal", "gloss": "Job search goal.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "food", "gloss": "Food.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "nutrition", "gloss": "Nutrition.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "meal", "gloss": "Meal structure.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "medical_topic", "gloss": "Medical topic.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "medical_audience", "gloss": "Medical audience.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "message_structure", "gloss": "Message structure.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "collaboration_structure", "gloss": "Collaboration structure.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "color", "gloss": "Product color.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "size", "gloss": "Product/garment size.", "nl_synonyms": []}, {"symbol": "gender", "gloss": "Demographic-audience facet.", "nl_synonyms": []}], "membership_rule": "Each attribute resolves to exactly one governing rule: target -> entity-name for ACTION/UTTER, artifact-value for GENERATE; destination/source/location/origin -> entity-name or location-name; relation -> spatial-relation; recipient/audience -> recipient-value; tone -> tone-value; format -> format-value; style/locale/modifier/state/metric -> descriptive-value; duration_unit -> duration-unit-value; currency -> currency-value; color/size/gender -> product-attribute-value; genre/category/availability/rank_field/rank_direction -> search-value; platform -> platform-name; duration/quantity/limit/min_rating/max_price/passengers/distance/travel_time/stop_count -> NUMBER; deadline/execution_date/date/return_date/showtime -> ISO_DATE or UTC_TIMESTAMP; itinerary/route -> LIST[STRING] of entity-name/location-name symbols (transitional element form pending a dedicated category); content/file/method/property/call/assertion/expected_output/actual_output/reproduction_step/policy/amenity/venue/ticket/seat/compatibility/revision/procedure/safety/escalation/academic_goal/job_search_goal/food/nutrition/meal/medical_topic/medical_audience/message_structure/collaboration_structure remain transitional STRING payloads: each is a tracked vocabulary gap (per N2/N8), explicitly retained here rather than silently dropped, pending a dedicated category in a future sprint.", "worked_example": {"nl": "Send an urgent email to the manager, then check if they replied by Friday.", "braincode": "ACTION send_email(recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_urgent, content=\"status update request\")\nACTION check_replied(target=role_manager, deadline=\"2025-06-06T23:59:59Z\") -> replied : BOOL"}, "change_type": "MAJOR", "rationale": "Restores every previously-listed attribute (nothing silently deleted), resolves the target contradiction by making the mapping construct-sensitive, fixes the invalid format=format_plain_text on send_email (removed, since send_email's signature never allowed format), and gives every attribute a traceable governing rule as N3 requires.", "cites_source": "HTML", "addresses_note": "N3"}], "_provider_used": "anthropic", "_model_used": "claude-sonnet-5"}
Critic assessment: {"decision": "needs-rework", "kpi_assessment": {"coverage": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Dedicated tone, duration-unit, currency, recipient, artifact, and product-facet categories improve coverage for several existing request shapes. However, sampled closed tasks still lack signature-permitted attributes and value categories for shape, product construction/state, itinerary constraints, walking-time constraints, source/link requests, and structured code facts; product-attribute-value is not wired into search_web, so its example is not statically valid."}, "expressivity": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Generate.target is correctly distinguished from Action.target, and role/tone/currency values preserve more intent than quoted adjectives. But held-trip-1 loses its per-day temple and inter-stop walking constraints, shopping loses gray/round, and ALFRED tasks lose white/warm because relevant attributes are unavailable in Action signatures. Many values remain prose STRING payloads, which is retained during this build phase but means the proposed vocabulary does not yet structurally preserve their content."}, "determinism": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Removing duplicate role_, tone_, curr_, art_, and dom_day locations is a genuine deterministic improvement. Yet translators still have incompatible choices for unlisted values: format-value permits minting a token that is not yet a glossary member, descriptive-value is a residual bucket with broad dom_ membership, and absent Action signatures force one translator to omit a constraint while another emits an invalid attribute. The independent translations demonstrate this divergence on the mirror, trip, code, and conversational items."}, "interpretability": {"impact": "benefit", "reasoning": "The new dedicated value categories and exhaustive attribute index substantially improve lookupability over the prior mixed descriptive-value bucket. The stated construct-sensitive target rule is especially clarifying. Interpretability remains impaired by the residual descriptive-value bucket and by attribute names whose governing rule is merely transitional STRING rather than a descriptive category, but this is a net improvement."}, "improvement": {"impact": "mixed", "reasoning": "Canonical role, unit, currency, tone, and artifact symbols give a weaker model useful planning constraints. Conversely, unwired product values and broad STRING payload channels do not improve execution planning for the most complex sampled tasks, and invalid-looking examples can mislead a model into emitting attributes the Action signatures reject."}}, "simulations": [{"item_id": "held-trip-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "Plan a 3-day itinerary in Kyoto that includes at least one temple per day and avoids anything more than a 20-minute walk from the last stop.", "braincode": "GAP(\"No construct/category encodes a per-day temple cardinality constraint or a maximum walking duration from each preceding stop; GENERATE content would only preserve these as a STRING payload.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "artifact-value and duration-unit-value help express an itinerary artifact and three days, but the actionable constraints have no symbolic representation."}, {"item_id": "held-support-1", "source": "seed_tasks", "nl": "If the customer's order is late and they're a first-time buyer, offer a 10% discount; if they're a repeat buyer, offer free expedited shipping instead.", "braincode": "GAP(\"No defined checks or attribute categories represent order lateness, first-time versus repeat buyer status, percentage discount, or customer-order relation.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "Flow-If supplies sequencing, but the required condition facts and numeric discount semantics are missing."}, {"item_id": "6ca55141-9ba6-4ed7-8c07-77df6c24029d", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Find the lowest-priced gray-colored round-shaped mirror in stock in Atlanta, Georgia, with a maximum price of 20 dollars.", "braincode": "GAP(\"search_web permits availability, currency, location, max_price but not color or shape; product-attribute-value is not in the search_web signature, and no shape category exists.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "currency-value and search-value help with dollars, stock, and cheapest ordering; color_gray would be allowed by the category rule but not by the Action signature."}, {"item_id": "62806bef-eeeb-4892-b4d5-6a8d2005c58d", "source": "Mind2Web", "nl": "Browse the trending searches in Columbus.", "braincode": "GAP(\"No search category/value or Action signature represents trending searches; a STRING content payload would not supply a structured browsing objective.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "No proposed change addresses a trend/popularity search criterion."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190907_134455_194210#0", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Place a white cup with a knife in it on the counter in front of the toaster.", "braincode": "GAP(\"Action signatures do not permit color, and no valid mechanism identifies the white cup while preserving its color constraint.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "product-attribute-value adds color_white but is not legal on pick_up or place. The remaining knife-in-cup and placement relations are expressible."}, {"item_id": "trial_T20190908_185043_273617#2", "source": "ALFRED", "nl": "Put a warm coffee cup in the coffee maker.", "braincode": "GAP(\"No Action signature accepts state=state_warm or another construction/state constraint; encoding heat then place preserves the process but cannot confirm the requested warm state symbolically.\")", "coverage": "Fail", "notes": "The existing heat/place sequence can approximate the request, but state_warm is absent and state is not signature-permitted."}, {"item_id": "pydata__xarray-4356", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix xarray sum so min_count works for reduction over more than one dimension, using the reported reproduction and proposed nanops.py change.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixXarraySum\nTASK FixXarraySum {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=code, actual_output=\"sum with min_count errors for more than one dimension\", content=\"replace mask.shape[axis] with np.take(a.shape, axis).prod()\", expected_output=\"min_count works over multiple dimensions\", file=\"xarray/core/nanops.py\", method=\"sum\", reproduction_step=\"da.sum([dim_0, dim_1], min_count=1)\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Action supports the software fields, but every substantive code/path/reproduction value remains a transitional STRING payload rather than a glossary category."}, {"item_id": "django__django-12155", "source": "SWE-bench_Verified", "nl": "Fix Django admindoc rendering when a docstring's first line is non-empty by skipping the first line when computing indentation.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FixDjangoDocstring\nTASK FixDjangoDocstring {\n  ACTION modify_code(target=code, actual_output=\"trim_docstring errors when the first docstring line is non-empty\", content=\"skip the first line in indentation calculation\", expected_output=\"render non-empty-first-line docstrings\", file=\"django/contrib/admindocs/utils.py\", method=\"trim_docstring\")\n  ACTION modify_code(target=code, file=\"django/contrib/admindocs/views.py\", content=\"update related admindoc handling\")\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The multi-file ordering is represented, but source code, paths, and expected behavior remain STRING content."}, {"item_id": "c892", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "The people in our country say that we are generous and warm, but I think people will take advantage of others; I feel I was born in the wrong country and ask for suggestions.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT GenerosityConcern\nCONVO GenerosityConcern {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"People may take advantage of others despite claims of generosity and warmth.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n  TURN t2 SPEAKER=USER REPLY_TO t1 {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Give suggestions for finding people or groups that are a better fit.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Conversation sequencing and speech acts are preserved, but the substantive emotional and advisory content remains STRING, violating N3's eventual value-set objective."}, {"item_id": "c5375", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "Can I swap my old phone for a new one?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT PhoneTradeIn\nCONVO PhoneTradeIn {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Can I trade in my old phone for a new phone?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The ask and recipient are represented; trade-in, old/new ownership, and phone details remain prose."}, {"item_id": "c2151", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "How did racism start, and how did it become a problem despite earlier acceptance of homosexuality?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT RacismHistoryQuestion\nCONVO RacismHistoryQuestion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Explain historical origins of racism and changing treatment of homosexuality.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Speech-act metadata is expressible, but the historical comparison is only a STRING payload."}, {"item_id": "c1195", "source": "PRISM", "nl": "I believe love in any relationship should be reciprocal and not one-sided.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ReciprocalLoveView\nCONVO ReciprocalLoveView {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"Love in a relationship should be reciprocal rather than one-sided.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The opinion speech act is captured, but no category structures relationship, reciprocity, or the stated proposition."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-38835", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Create a newsletter of up to 800 words from the supplied applied-observability article.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT AppliedObservabilityNewsletter\nCONVO AppliedObservabilityNewsletter {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Create a newsletter from the supplied applied-observability article, with a maximum of 800 words.\", recipient=role_agent, tone=tone_professional)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "recipient-value and tone-value help, but there is no length attribute on UTTER and newsletter/article/source content is a STRING payload."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-111541", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Give another catchy Hinglish SEO title, description, and comma-separated tags for a YouTube Short about Vivek Bindra discussing whether AI will take jobs.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT YouTubeShortSEO\nCONVO YouTubeShortSEO {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Generate another catchy Hinglish SEO title, description, and comma-separated tags about AI taking jobs.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The request act is represented, but language, SEO keywords, title/description/tags structure, and content remain untyped prose."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-55500", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Continue Part 2 of the Donatello and Goku battle story.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ContinueDonatelloStory\nCONVO ContinueDonatelloStory {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Continue Part 2 of the Donatello and Goku battle story.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The continuation request is captured as an ask, but character, part, narrative, and transformation constraints remain STRING text."}, {"item_id": "wildchat1m_en3u-30875", "source": "PATHs", "nl": "Which U.S. state does not require a work permit for non-U.S. citizens?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT WorkPermitQuestion\nCONVO WorkPermitQuestion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Which U.S. state does not require a work permit for non-U.S. citizens?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The information request is captured, but jurisdiction, immigration status, and work-permit concepts lack categories."}, {"item_id": "1775708977070", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Suggest a warm light midnight snack that supports satiety and portion control.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT MidnightSnackAdvice\nCONVO MidnightSnackAdvice {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Suggest a warm light midnight snack for satiety and portion control.\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "No food, temperature, nutrition, satiety, or portion-control value category exists; these are explicitly tracked STRING gaps."}, {"item_id": "1775686840693", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Can foot fungus spread to the groin or buttocks?", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT FungalSpreadQuestion\nCONVO FungalSpreadQuestion {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER ask(content=\"Can foot fungus spread to the groin or buttocks?\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "The question act is encoded, but medical topic, affected body sites, and transmission relation remain prose."}, {"item_id": "1775962320176", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Hello", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT Greeting\nCONVO Greeting {\n  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {\n    UTTER inform(content=\"Hello\", recipient=role_agent)\n  }\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "Even this simple greeting requires transitional STRING content because no greeting speech-act/content symbol is defined."}, {"item_id": "1775436940555", "source": "ThoughtTrace", "nl": "Suggest a friendly email to my boss asking to resume work after a week absent due to illness.", "braincode": "ENTRYPOINT ResumeWorkEmail\nTASK ResumeWorkEmail : STRING {\n  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, audience=role_manager, content=\"Write a friendly email requesting return to work after one week absent due to illness.\", format=format_email, tone=tone_polite) -> short_text : STRING\n  RETURN short_text\n}", "coverage": "Partial", "notes": "artifact-value, recipient-value, format-value, and tone-value improve the request metadata, but illness, absence, return-to-work intent, and email substance remain STRING."}], "cross_check": {"used": true, "agreement": "low", "notes": "Anthropic marks gaps for the trip, mirror, ALFRED, code, and open requests, while Gemini frequently emits attributes or symbols unsupported by the current Action signatures and glossary categories (for example color on search_web and white_cup). This supports the finding that the vocabulary/signature boundary is not yet deterministic."}, "required_changes": [{"target": "Action", "change": "Revise operation signatures atomically with the new product vocabulary: add color, size, and gender where product search/filtering actually permits them, or remove the product-attribute-value worked example until that wiring exists. Add a separate shape attribute and shape-value category before claiming support for round-product searches."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "Replace the residual mappings `style/locale/modifier/state/metric -> descriptive-value` with dedicated value categories or precise prefix-specific subcategory rules. A value such as a locale, style, or support metric must have a defined symbolic membership rule, not merely be sent to a bucket whose prefixes cover only mod_, state_, and dom_."}, {"target": "format-value", "change": "Make validity consistent with N2/N3: either define the complete category as rule-derived and state that every matching format_ token is glossary-derived immediately, or require prior glossary membership and prohibit minting in expressions. Do not say both that new symbols are permitted and that they are only recorded next sprint."}, {"target": "vocabulary basis", "change": "Add missing categories and Action wiring required by the closed samples: shape; object color/state on household objects; construction/difficulty and production/yield; source/link request; popularity/trending search; itinerary stop/day, per-day cardinality, and walking-duration constraints; and customer/order status plus percentage-discount values."}, {"target": "attribute-name", "change": "For every transitional STRING attribute, add a concrete N2 vocabulary-gap category and a defined migration target rather than treating broad semantic fields such as file, method, policy, medical_topic, food, and message_structure as value sets governed only by STRING. Retaining STRING is allowed in this build phase, but it does not satisfy N3 and must be explicitly narrowed category-by-category."}, {"target": "Types & Lexicon / attribute-name", "change": "Define the static type of glossary value symbols and list elements. The rule `itinerary/route -> LIST[STRING] of entity-name/location-name symbols` conflicts with value typing because an unquoted symbol is syntactically IDENT, not a STRING literal."}], "logic_issues": ["product-attribute-value's worked example is statically invalid: search_web's normative signature does not permit color, size, or gender.", "No shape attribute or shape-value category exists, so the sampled gray round mirror request cannot be represented even after adding product color values.", "format-value's rule permits a translator to mint an unlisted token but says the token is recorded only next sprint; this conflicts with the claim that values are glossary symbols or immediately glossary-rule-derived.", "The attribute-name rule calls descriptive-value the governing category for style, locale, and metric even though descriptive-value's normative membership rule only recognizes mod_, state_, and dom_ symbols.", "The proposed Generate grammar still admits generic `value`, while its semantics restrict individual attributes; a static validation rule is needed to reject otherwise grammatical but category-invalid values consistently.", "The itinerary/route list rule claims LIST[STRING] elements can be entity-name/location-name symbols, but the language's type system does not define such bare symbols as STRING values."], "notes_assessment": {"N2": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Six dedicated descriptive categories and a fuller attribute index are real vocabulary growth, but large descriptive domains and several sampled task concepts still have no category."}, "N3": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "tone, duration_unit, currency, recipient/audience, Generate target, format, and product facets now have much clearer governing sets, and duplicate values were removed. However, many listed attributes still accept transitional STRING phrases, several residual mappings have no precise value rule, and some new values are not legal in their consuming Action signatures."}, "N7": {"status": "violated", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Canonical-category de-duplication and Generate ordering improve convergence. Remaining arbitrary minting, residual buckets, and signature/category mismatches still lead independent translators to incompatible valid/invalid encodings."}, "N1": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "STRING and free IDENT channels remain intentionally available during the build phase; the proposal does not close them."}, "N4": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "The proposal explicitly retains content and many other values as natural-language STRING payloads, as permitted before the later closing phase."}, "N5": {"status": "violated", "trend": "unchanged", "reasoning": "Expressions still rely on free STRING prose and open identifiers whose semantic segmentation is not wholly glossary-defined."}, "N6": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "The new categories are grammar-oriented and artifact-value explicitly invokes the complete-glossary assumption. Missing categories for shape, trip constraints, and several other sampled concepts still prevent applying that assumption."}, "N8": {"status": "partial", "trend": "improved", "reasoning": "Fine-grained tones, units, currencies, formats, roles, and product facets preserve more distinctions. Important closed-task distinctions remain absent or unwired, so richness is still materially constrained."}}, "rebuttal_rulings": [], "accept_changes": ["Flow-If", "tone-value", "duration-unit-value", "currency-value", "recipient-value", "artifact-value", "descriptive-value", "search-value", "product-attribute-value"], "chosen_position": null, "position_comparison": null, "reasoning": "This bundle makes meaningful N3 progress by separating several attribute value sets, fixing the Generate target contradiction, and eliminating duplicate canonical symbols. It cannot be accepted as a whole because category validity and Action signatures are not aligned, the format rule remains internally inconsistent, and broad residual/STRING mappings do not yet give many attributes a precise symbolic governing rule. The listed self-contained vocabulary and Flow-If changes can land now without depending on the broken mappings or signature revisions."}
