Proposed changes available for this translation:
- [revise] Types & Lexicon: grammar `type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" type "]" | "REF" "[" type "]"
value ::= STRING | NUMBER | IDENT | "TRUE" | "FALSE" | list_lit | diff
list_lit ::= "[" value ("," value)* "]"
diff ::= IDENT "-" NUMBER
IDENT ::= [a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*
STRING ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\n] | "\\\"" | "\\\\" | "\\n" | "\\t" | "\\u" HEXHEXHEXHEX )* "\""
NUMBER ::= "-"? [0-9]+ ( "." [0-9]+ )? ( ("e"|"E") ("+"|"-")? [0-9]+ )?
COMMENT ::= "#" through end of physical line.` — As before, with one addition: a bare IDENT token that names a member of a defined vocabulary category (e.g. `role_manager`, `tone_urgent`, `art_itinerary`) is a **vocabulary symbol**. Lexically it is an IDENT (unquoted, no STRING escaping), but for all static typing purposes — RETURN type matching, LET's exact-type rule, Check comparisons, and LIST[T] element typing — a vocabulary symbol has static type STRING. This resolves the prior inconsistency where `LIST[STRING]` was declared to hold bare category symbols (e.g. itinerary stops as entity-name/location-name members) despite IDENT and STRING being distinct value forms: the rule makes that legal and precise rather than contradictory. A vocabulary symbol is never a STRING *literal* (it carries no quotes and cannot use string escapes) but it type-checks as STRING wherever STRING is required. Everything else in Types & Lexicon (REF[T], the four base types, `diff`) is unchanged.
- [revise] Generate: grammar `generation ::= "GENERATE" "(" generate-attr ("," generate-attr)* ")" "->" IDENT ":" gen_type
generate-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
gen_type ::= "NUMBER" | "STRING" | "BOOL" | "LIST" "[" gen_type "]"` — Legal Generate attributes: target, audience, content, duration, duration_unit, format, locale, quantity, style, tone, stop_min_per_day, max_walk_duration, max_walk_duration_unit. `target`'s value is an artifact-value symbol (GENERATE always produces an artifact, never an entity; Action.target stays entity-name/artifact-value split by construct, not by attribute name). `audience` -> recipient-value. `tone` -> tone-value. `format` -> format-value. `duration_unit`/`max_walk_duration_unit` -> duration-unit-value. `style` -> style-value. `locale` -> locale-value. `duration`, `quantity`, `stop_min_per_day`, `max_walk_duration` are NUMBER. `stop_min_per_day` expresses a minimum-count-per-day constraint (e.g. at least one temple per day); `max_walk_duration`+`max_walk_duration_unit` express a maximum-walking-time-between-stops constraint. Canonical ordering: target first, then optional attributes alphabetically. Handle rule unchanged. `content` remains a transitional STRING channel pending N4.
- [revise] Action: grammar `action ::= "ACTION" operation-id "(" action-attrs? ")" ("->" IDENT ":" type)?
action-attrs ::= action-attr ("," action-attr)*
action-attr ::= attribute-name "=" value
operation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member

-- Updated/added signatures (others unchanged from prior sprint):
-- search_web(target, [availability, category, color, currency, genre, gender, location, max_price, min_rating, platform, shape, size, trending]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]
-- pick_up(target, [source, color, shape, state]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]
-- place(target, destination, [location, relation, state]) -> NONE
-- browse_trending(target, [location]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]
-- offer_discount(target, [content, discount_percent]) -> NONE
-- check_support_status(target, metric) -> BOOL [VALUE]` — Unchanged validation rule (attribute must be a governed attribute-name member, category-valid, and signature-listed) plus these wirings: `color`/`size`/`gender` (product-attribute-value) and `shape` (shape-value, new) are now legal on `search_web` and `pick_up` so product search/selection can carry physical descriptors (e.g. a gray round mirror). `state` (state-value, new) is legal on `pick_up` and `place` so an object's required or resulting condition (warm, clean, microwaved) can be asserted when selecting/placing it, without requiring an extra heat/rinse step when the object is merely being identified by state. `browse_trending` is a new operation for browsing a platform's currently-popular items/searches by location; its `target` is an entity-name symbol for the thing browsed (e.g. `trending_searches`, pending addition — quoted-string transitional exception applies per entity-name's rule until added). `discount_percent` (NUMBER, 0-100) is now legal on `offer_discount` to express a percentage discount. `check_support_status`'s `metric` attribute now also accepts order/customer-status members from the expanded metric-value category (e.g. order lateness, first-time vs. repeat buyer), so conditional support logic can branch on them via Check/Flow-If. Canonical ordering and handle rules are unchanged.
- [add vocabulary] shape-value (closed): The closed set of geometric-shape symbols usable wherever an attribute calls for an object's shape (Action's shape attribute). Members: shape_round, shape_square, shape_rectangular, shape_oval, shape_triangular
- [add vocabulary] state-value (open): Canonical symbols for a physical object's condition or state, used with Action's state attribute (selecting, confirming, or producing an object in a given condition). Members: state_warm, state_cold, state_microwaved, state_clean, state_dirty; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `state_[a-z_]+` naming a physical condition an entity can be in or be required to be in. New states are added as new members, never as free text.
- [add vocabulary] style-value (open): Canonical writing/production style symbols for GENERATE's style attribute. Members: style_narrative, style_technical, style_academic, style_persuasive, style_catchy; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `style_[a-z_]+` naming a compositional/rhetorical style. New styles are added as new members, never as free text.
- [add vocabulary] locale-value (open): Canonical language/region locale symbols for GENERATE's locale attribute. Members: locale_en_us, locale_en_gb, locale_hi_en, locale_es, locale_fr; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `locale_[a-z_]+` naming a language/region variant. New locales are added as new members, never as free text.
- [add vocabulary] metric-value (open): Canonical symbols for a queryable status metric, used with check_support_status's metric attribute — covering both service-support metrics and order/customer status facts. Members: metric_uptime, metric_response_time, metric_compatibility, metric_order_late, metric_first_time_buyer, metric_repeat_buyer; membership rule: An atomic symbol matching `metric_[a-z_]+` naming a boolean-queryable status fact. New metrics are added as new members, never as free text.
