   "addresses_note": "N3"
  },
  {
   "op": "revise",
   "construct_name": "Action",
   "grammar": "action ::= \"ACTION\" operation-id \"(\" action-attrs? \")\" (\"->\" IDENT \":\" type)?\naction-attrs ::= action-attr (\",\" action-attr)*\naction-attr ::= attribute-name \"=\" value\noperation-id ::= operation-vocabulary member\n\n-- Updated/added signatures (others unchanged from prior sprint):\n-- search_web(target, [availability, category, color, currency, genre, gender, location, max_price, min_rating, platform, shape, size, trending]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- pick_up(target, [source, color, shape, state]) -> REF[STRING] [SAME]\n-- place(target, destination, [location, relation, state]) -> NONE\n-- browse_trending(target, [location]) -> LIST[REF[STRING]] [NEW]\n-- offer_discount(target, [content, discount_percent]) -> NONE\n-- check_support_status(target, metric) -> BOOL [VALUE]",
   "semantics": "Unchanged validation rule (attribute must be a governed attribute-name member, category-valid, and signature-listed) plus these wirings: `color`/`size`/`gender` (product-attribute-value) and `shape` (shape-value, new) are now legal on `search_web` and `pick_up` so product search/selection can carry physical descriptors (e.g. a gray round mirror). `state` (state-value, new) is legal on `pick_up` and `place` so an object's required or resulting condition (warm, clean, microwaved) can be asserted when selecting/placing it, without requiring an extra heat/rinse step when the object is merely being identified by state. `browse_trending` is a new operation for browsing a platform's currently-popular items/searches by location; its `target` is an entity-name symbol for the thing browsed (e.g. `trending_searches`, pending addition — quoted-string transitional exception applies per entity-name's rule until added). `discount_percent` (NUMBER, 0-100) is now legal on `offer_discount` to express a percentage discount. `check_support_status`'s `metric` attribute now also accepts order/customer-status members from the expanded metric-value category (e.g. order lateness, first-time vs. repeat buyer), so conditional support logic can branch on them via Check/Flow-If. Canonical ordering and handle rules are unchanged.",
   "worked_example": {
    "nl": "Find the lowest-priced gray round mirror in stock in Atlanta, under $20.",
    "braincode": "ACTION search_web(target=mirror, color=color_gray, shape=shape_round, availability=avail_in_stock, location=atlanta, currency=curr_usd, max_price=20) -> mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]\nACTION sort(target=mirrors, rank_field=rank_price, rank_direction=dir_asc) -> sorted_mirrors : LIST[REF[STRING]]"
   },
   "glossary_gloss": "Action's per-operation attribute lists now actually include the physical descriptors (color, size, gender, shape, state) and the new trending-browse and percentage-discount attributes that requests need, instead of leaving them valid by category but rejected by signature.",
   "change_type": "MAJOR",
   "rationale": "Directly resolves the Critic's core objection: product-attribute-value and the new shape/state categories are useless if no Action signature admits them. Wiring them into search_web/pick_up/place, and adding browse_trending and discount_percent, closes the gray-round-mirror, warm-cup, white-cup, trending-search, and order-discount gaps.",
   "cites_source": "HTML",
   "addresses_note": "N3"
  },
