   "assistant: # Dinner Plan for 4 🍽️\n\nWith pork chops, rice, and baked beans, you have a **great classic comfort meal** ready to go!\n\n---\n\n## 🥩 Main: Pan-Seared or Baked Pork Chops\n**Simple seasoning ideas:**\n- Salt, pepper, garlic powder, paprika\n- Sear in a pan with butter for a nice crust\n- Or bake at 400°F for about 20-25 minutes\n\n---\n\n## 🍚 Side 1: Seasoned Rice\n- Cook with **chicken broth instead of water** for extra flavor\n- Add a little butter and garlic\n- Takes about 20 minutes\n\n---\n\n## 🫘 Side 2: Baked Beans\n- Heat on the stove or in the oven\n- You can **add a little brown sugar, bacon bits, or mustard** to dress them up\n\n---\n\n## ⏱️ Timeline\n| Time | Task |\n|------|------|\n| 6:00 | Start rice & preheat oven |\n| 6:15 | Season & sear pork chops |\n| 6:20 | Heat baked beans |\n| 6:40 | Everything ready to serve! |\n\n---\n\n**You'll be done well within your 2 hours!** 🎉\n\nWould you like specific recipes for any of these?",
