KPI assessment: {'coverage': {'impact': 'benefit', 'reasoning': 'The added shape, state, metric, locale, style, itinerary, browsing, and discount facilities cover several previously unsupported held-out constraints, including round mirrors, full/empty rolls, support discounts, and itinerary timing. However, the proposed stop_min_per_day attribute records only a number and cannot state that the required daily stop is a temple, while several code and content attributes remain opaque STRING payloads.'}, 'expressivity': {'impact': 'mixed', 'reasoning': 'The proposal adds first-class fields for several constraints previously hidden in content, but its itinerary example still loses the required temple category: stop_min_per_day=1 means only a count. Transitional STRING attributes continue to carry code paths, expected outcomes, policies, message structure, and substantive generation requests as prose rather than defined value sets.'}, 'determinism': {'impact': 'mixed', 'reasoning': 'Dedicated value categories and the closed-for-encoding format rule improve convergence. Yet independent translations still diverge materially on TASK versus CONVO, target selection, status-query sequencing, artifact type, return type, and handle names; the new open categories also lack exhaustive synonym/canonicalization rules. The worked examples themselves violate the stated canonical attribute ordering.'}, 'interpretability': {'impact': 'mixed', 'reasoning': 'Splitting state/style/locale/metric out of descriptive-value makes values easier to look up. But attribute-name calls itself a complete index while retaining dozens of unresolved future categories, and the duplicate add of the already-existing descriptive-value entry is structurally unclear. The overloaded rule that every vocabulary symbol statically counts as STRING also obscures category identity in general typed contexts.'}, 'improvement': {'impact': 'benefit', 'reasoning': 'A weaker planner gains useful actionable structure from color, shape, state, discount percentage, support metrics, and numeric itinerary constraints. It still cannot reliably act on semantic constraints hidden in STRING content, such as the private-members feature behavior, the exact temple requirement, or a user-provided script that must be revised.'}}
